admin-settings-help-reader-actions-block-sender = Choose toolbar, More menu or hidden. Feature restrictions, permissions and message context still apply. Users can choose unless this is locked.
admin-settings-key-reader-action-style = Message action ribbon
admin-settings-help-reader-action-style = Compact icons are the default. Choose labels for icons with visible text; both retain action names and themed tooltips. Supports global, domain and user policy locks.
admin-settings-key-nextcloud-sync-interval-secs = Nextcloud automatic refresh interval
admin-settings-help-nextcloud-sync-interval-secs = Seconds between background collection refreshes for connected native-engine accounts. Zero is manual only; positive values have a sixty-second minimum. Failures back off. No background sign-in is attempted.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-inbox = Inbox folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-inbox = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-drafts = Drafts folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-drafts = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-sent = Sent folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-sent = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-trash = Trash folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-trash = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-junk = Junk folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-junk = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-role-archive = Archive folder mapping
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-role-archive = Null uses automatic discovery. Use an exact path object for shared defaults or an owned mailbox ID object for one account. Missing or conflicting targets disable this role; administrator locks apply.

admin-settings-key-mail-request-delivery-receipt = Request delivery notifications by default
admin-settings-help-mail-request-delivery-receipt = Select delivery notifications for new messages when the account supports SMTP DSN. Locking controls this saved default; receipts.dsnAllowed separately governs whether requests are permitted. Delivery does not prove reading.

admin-settings-key-security-signin-geo-enforce-sessions = Enforce country policy on existing sessions
admin-settings-help-security-signin-geo-enforce-sessions = Off by default. Apply the configured sign-in country scope to authenticated requests, native bearer access and signed reader content. Blocked clients can still sign out. Already-open streams are checked when they reconnect; this does not terminate existing connections.

admin-settings-key-security-protection-rate-mode = Aggregate request budgets
admin-settings-help-security-protection-rate-mode = Off by default. Observe records budget exhaustion without refusal; enforce returns a temporary 429. Existing protocol concurrency limits remain independent.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-adaptive-mode = Adaptive request protection
admin-settings-help-security-protection-adaptive-mode = Off by default. Observe records explainable typed anomalies and proposed actions; enforce applies bounded temporary throttles or blocks. This is a deterministic counter policy, not an AI classifier.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-client-requests = Client requests per window
admin-settings-help-security-protection-client-requests = Requests per window from one address that is not signed in, and every sign-in request. A request with a valid mailbox or admin session uses its own, larger allowance instead. Zero turns this budget off.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-account-requests = Account requests per window
admin-settings-help-security-protection-account-requests = Requests per window for one signed-in mailbox, across its sessions, devices and addresses. Kept above the anonymous allowance so signed-in use has more room. Zero turns this budget off.
admin-settings-key-rate-limit-diagnostics-burst = Diagnostic runs at once
admin-settings-help-rate-limit-diagnostics-burst = Diagnostic runs and backend checks an admin session may start in a row. Starting a check that is already running returns that check instead of counting again.
admin-settings-key-rate-limit-diagnostics-per-minute = Diagnostic runs per minute
admin-settings-help-rate-limit-diagnostics-per-minute = Diagnostic runs and backend checks per minute an admin session regains.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-admin-requests = Admin requests per window
admin-settings-help-security-protection-admin-requests = Requests per window for one signed-in administrator. Kept above the anonymous allowance. Zero turns this budget off.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-rate-window-secs = Request budget window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-rate-window-secs = Fixed request-budget interval. Capacity load shedding and ordinary not-found responses are not adaptive evidence.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-adaptive-clients = Observe clients for adaptive protection
admin-settings-help-security-protection-adaptive-clients = Enable this subject dimension when adaptive mode is active. Accounts and administrators are counted only after their identity is verified.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-adaptive-accounts = Observe accounts for adaptive protection
admin-settings-help-security-protection-adaptive-accounts = Enable this subject dimension when adaptive mode is active. Accounts and administrators are counted only after their identity is verified.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-adaptive-admins = Observe admins for adaptive protection
admin-settings-help-security-protection-adaptive-admins = Enable this subject dimension when adaptive mode is active. Accounts and administrators are counted only after their identity is verified.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-short-window-secs = Short anomaly window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-short-window-secs = Rolling observation window. Long windows support hours through thirty days; bucket rounding can retain at most one extra sixty-fourth of a window.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-short-minimum-samples = Short ratio minimum samples
admin-settings-help-security-protection-short-minimum-samples = Minimum observed normal plus anomalous requests before the ratio trigger applies. The absolute anomaly threshold is independent of this minimum.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-short-absolute-anomalies = Short absolute anomaly budget
admin-settings-help-security-protection-short-absolute-anomalies = Trigger when this many selected anomalies accumulate, even when normal requests dilute the ratio. Zero disables this trigger.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-short-ratio-percent = Short anomaly ratio (percent)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-short-ratio-percent = Trigger when selected anomalies reach this percentage after the minimum sample count. Either the absolute or ratio trigger suffices. Zero disables this trigger.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-long-window-secs = Long anomaly window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-long-window-secs = Rolling observation window. Long windows support hours through thirty days; bucket rounding can retain at most one extra sixty-fourth of a window.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-long-minimum-samples = Long ratio minimum samples
admin-settings-help-security-protection-long-minimum-samples = Minimum observed normal plus anomalous requests before the ratio trigger applies. The absolute anomaly threshold is independent of this minimum.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-long-absolute-anomalies = Long absolute anomaly budget
admin-settings-help-security-protection-long-absolute-anomalies = Trigger when this many selected anomalies accumulate, even when normal requests dilute the ratio. Zero disables this trigger.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-long-ratio-percent = Long anomaly ratio (percent)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-long-ratio-percent = Trigger when selected anomalies reach this percentage after the minimum sample count. Either the absolute or ratio trigger suffices. Zero disables this trigger.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-normal-cap-per-bucket = Normal baseline cap per bucket
admin-settings-help-security-protection-normal-cap-per-bucket = Bound the normal baseline learned in each rolling-window bucket. Independent absolute anomaly budgets prevent unlimited valid-request padding from hiding abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-signals = Adaptive evidence signals
admin-settings-help-security-protection-signals = Select authoritative malformed, oversized, credential-rejected, permission-denied, body-deadline or opt-in admin-route-miss observations. Admin route probing excludes entity-not-found responses and static assets; generic status codes, capacity refusals and user-agent strings do not establish abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-throttle-secs = Initial temporary throttle (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-throttle-secs = First threshold crossing starts a fixed throttle deadline. Requests during that deadline do not extend it.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-block-secs = Escalated temporary block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-block-secs = A later threshold crossing before recovery may escalate to this bounded block. No permanent account lock is created.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-decay-secs = Quiet recovery interval (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-decay-secs = After this anomaly-free interval and expiry of the current action, escalation returns to its initial stage. Rolling evidence expires according to its configured windows.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-exempt-clients = Exempt client addresses and networks
admin-settings-help-security-protection-exempt-clients = Exact IP addresses or CIDR networks exempt only the client dimension. Verified account limits still apply. Use deliberately for shared NAT networks; forwarded addresses are trusted only through configured proxies.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-exempt-accounts = Exempt verified account IDs
admin-settings-help-security-protection-exempt-accounts = Exact server-verified mailbox account IDs exempt only their account dimension, never the source-client dimension. Email addresses and caller-supplied account parameters are not identity evidence.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-exempt-admins = Exempt administrator IDs
admin-settings-help-security-protection-exempt-admins = Exact authenticated administrator IDs exempt only their administrator dimension. Existing sign-in failure locks and strict administrator session deadlines remain unchanged.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-storage-failure = Enforcement storage failure policy
admin-settings-help-security-protection-storage-failure = Closed refuses protected work when an enabled enforcement budget cannot be checked. Open temporarily permits it with a bounded operational warning. Observe-only failures never impose an enforcement action.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-enabled = Admin-probe protection
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-enabled = Count requests that look for the admin console per client network (IPv4 address, IPv6 /64), slow a source that keeps going, then block it. Typos and stale bookmarks stay inside the grace allowance. Changed in Security > Adaptive protection.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-grace-allowance = Grace allowance (misses per window)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-grace-allowance = Misses ignored per window. The score drains continuously at this many points per window.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-window-secs = Grace window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-window-secs = The window the grace allowance applies to.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-block-after = Misses beyond grace before a block
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-block-after = Misses above the grace allowance that start a block. Misses in between are answered after the tarpit delay.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-tarpit-delay-ms = Tarpit delay (ms)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-tarpit-delay-ms = Delay added to each counted miss above the grace allowance. 0 turns the tarpit off. Other requests are never delayed.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-block-secs = First block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-block-secs = Length of the first block. A blocked source gets the same answer for every path.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-max-block-secs = Longest block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-max-block-secs = A repeat block doubles the previous length, up to this cap.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-repeat-window-secs = Repeat window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-repeat-window-secs = A block that starts within this long after the previous one ended counts as a repeat.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-block-status = Blocked answer status
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-block-status = HTTP status sent to a blocked source, with Retry-After: 429 or 403.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-signals = Counted misses
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-signals = probe-path, slug-guess (a 404 at the console's path depth), admin-signin-failed and admin-unauthenticated.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-probe-paths = Probe paths
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-probe-paths = Paths scanners ask for, such as /wp-admin or /.env. A path that contains one as whole segments counts as a miss. The console's own path never does.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-allowlist = Never-blocked networks
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-allowlist = IP addresses or CIDR networks (office, VPN) that are never counted or blocked.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-audit-ip = Source address in the audit log
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-audit-ip = masked shows IPv4 /24 and IPv6 /48; full shows the address. The fail2ban line always has the full address.
admin-settings-key-security-admin-probe-fail2ban-log = fail2ban log line on block
admin-settings-help-security-admin-probe-fail2ban-log = Write one mailwoman[admin-probe] line with rhost=<address> when a source is blocked.

admin-settings-key-appearance-custom-css-enabled = Allow personal appearance CSS
admin-settings-help-appearance-custom-css-enabled = Allow restricted visual styles in the owner’s workspace. Disabled by default; enforced mailbox appearance locks pause these styles.
admin-settings-key-appearance-custom-js-enabled = Allow personal appearance scripts
admin-settings-help-appearance-custom-js-enabled = Allow isolated scripts that can only request appearance changes. Disabled by default; scripts cannot access mail, account data, or the application DOM.

admin-settings-key-mail-modifier-selection = Message modifier-key selection
admin-settings-help-mail-modifier-selection = Allow Ctrl, Command and Shift range selection. Lock this value to enforce it; visible selection controls remain available.
admin-settings-key-mail-drag-to-folder = Drag messages to folders
admin-settings-help-mail-drag-to-folder = Allow account-bound message dragging to real folders. This does not grant mailbox write permission; the server still authorizes each move.

admin-settings-key-admin-allow-last-superadmin-loss = Allow losing the last Super admin
admin-settings-help-admin-allow-last-superadmin-loss = Off by default. Enabling this permits later changes to remove the final Super admin access. A full Super admin must confirm the consequence with fresh authentication.
admin-settings-last-superadmin-title = Allow losing all Super admin access?
admin-settings-last-superadmin-body = Later account changes may leave nobody able to administer this deployment. Recovery would require local deployment administration. Type ALLOW LAST SUPERADMIN LOSS to enable this exception.
admin-settings-last-superadmin-confirm = Allow loss of access

admin-settings-key-mail-folder-counts = Folder counts
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-counts = Choose hidden, unread, unread only while there is unread mail, total, or both counts beside folders. Set global, domain, or user defaults, and lock the choice when required. Applies to every linked mailbox of an account.
admin-settings-key-mail-folder-count-scope = Folders with counts
admin-settings-help-mail-folder-count-scope = All folders, or only main folders (Inbox, Drafts, Sent, Archive, Junk, Trash, Outbox and other special-use folders). With main folders only, custom folders and their subfolders show no count. Applies to every linked mailbox of an account.
admin-settings-key-mail-compact-folder-badges = Compact secondary folder badges
admin-settings-help-mail-compact-folder-badges = Show smaller badges outside Inbox. Users can choose their own size unless this setting is locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-focused-inbox = Focused inbox
admin-settings-help-mail-focused-inbox = Split Inbox into Focused and Other tabs; newsletters and automated senders go to Other. Off by default. Users can turn it on or off in Settings > Folders and sidebar unless this setting is locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-account-unread-badge = Unread count beside the mailbox name
admin-settings-help-mail-account-unread-badge = Show the Inbox unread count next to the signed-in address or nickname in the sidebar. Off by default. The counts of other mailboxes in the mailbox menu are always shown. Applies to every linked mailbox of an account.

admin-settings-key-privacy-remote-image-downloads = Manual remote image downloads
admin-settings-key-privacy-remote-images-toast = Loading-images notification
admin-settings-help-privacy-remote-images-toast = Show one notification in the reader while a message's remote images load through the privacy proxy, and say when they have loaded or how many could not. On by default. Only changes what the reader shows; which images load is still decided by the remote content policy.
admin-settings-help-privacy-remote-image-downloads = Allow an explicit download of an image referenced by the owned message through the guarded privacy proxy. Disabled by default; this never opens the external URL directly.
admin-settings-key-privacy-sessions-show-linked-origin = Linked mailbox origin in sessions
admin-settings-help-privacy-sessions-show-linked-origin = How Settings > Security > Sessions names the account a Linked mailbox access session comes from: the full address, the address with the first part of the name masked, or nothing. The value is shown only to the owner of the sessions, never to other users. Default: full address.
admin-settings-key-mail-resume-tabs = Resume workspace tabs
admin-settings-help-mail-resume-tabs = Restore account-owned tab references after reload. Disabling this clears the local workspace record without deleting drafts.

admin-settings-key-metrics-default-range-seconds = Default request history range
admin-settings-help-metrics-default-range-seconds = Seconds shown when a history request does not specify a range. Limited by retention and the maximum range.
admin-settings-key-metrics-max-range-seconds = Maximum request history range
admin-settings-help-metrics-max-range-seconds = Maximum seconds per history query. Retention remains an additional limit.

admin-settings-key-contacts-favorites-first = Favorites first in suggestions
admin-settings-help-contacts-favorites-first = List favorite contacts ahead of other matches in recipient suggestions. Only the order changes; no suggestion is hidden. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-from-message-enabled = Save contacts from a message
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-from-message-enabled = Offer Save contacts from this message in message menus. When off the item is hidden. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-from-message-default-scope = Contacts ticked first when saving from a message
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-from-message-default-scope = Which participants are ticked first in the Save contacts dialog: the sender only, the sender and Reply-To, or everyone. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-from-message-skip-automated = Skip automated senders when saving contacts
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-from-message-skip-automated = Leave no-reply, notification and bounce addresses out of the Save contacts dialog unless ticked by hand. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-from-message-add-note = Note on contacts saved from a message
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-from-message-add-note = Add the note "Saved from a message on <date>" to contacts saved from a message. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-from-message-default-book = Address book for contacts saved from a message
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-from-message-default-book = The address book id that receives contacts saved from a message; "default" uses the default address book. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-sender-enabled = Save sender as contact
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-sender-enabled = Offer the one-click Save sender as contact item in message menus. When off the item is hidden. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-save-sender-use-reply-to = Save Reply-To for list senders
admin-settings-help-contacts-save-sender-use-reply-to = Save the Reply-To address instead of From when the sender is a mailing list or notification address. User and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-contacts-sender-icons = Bundled sender icons
admin-settings-help-contacts-sender-icons = Show locally bundled icons for recognised sender domains, with generated initials for others. Contact pictures take priority. Icons do not verify a sender's identity. No external logo service is contacted; user and domain overrides can be locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-brand-avatars = Brand logos beside verified senders
admin-settings-help-mail-brand-avatars = Show a locally bundled brand logo beside the sender when the sender's domain, or a subdomain of it, belongs to a known brand. See the authentication setting below for when a failed or missing check hides it. No logo is fetched from the sender or a logo service.
admin-settings-key-mail-brand-avatars-require-auth = Authentication needed for brand logos
admin-settings-help-mail-brand-avatars-require-auth = never: show a logo whenever the domain matches. known-failure (default): show it unless the message's cached DKIM or DMARC result is a failure; unchecked messages keep the logo. always: show it only after an aligned DMARC pass with DKIM for the brand's own domain. User and domain overrides can be locked.

admin-settings-key-mail-draft-save-mode = Account draft save mode
admin-settings-help-mail-draft-save-mode = Save after a typing pause, periodically, or only on demand. Saves require a supported upstream Drafts folder; uncertain writes are never automatically retried.
admin-settings-key-mail-draft-debounce-ms = Draft typing pause (milliseconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-draft-debounce-ms = Wait 500 to 10000 milliseconds after editing before saving in realtime mode.
admin-settings-key-mail-draft-interval-secs = Draft save interval (seconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-draft-interval-secs = Save edited drafts every 5 to 3600 seconds in periodic mode. Unchanged drafts are not written again.

admin-settings-key-login-remember-signins = Remember successful sign-in addresses
admin-settings-help-login-remember-signins = Keep up to ten successfully used usernames or email addresses on this device for the sign-in dropdown. Never saves passwords or sessions. Disabling removes this server's saved addresses when a device next loads the sign-in page or completes sign-in; it does not control the browser's own autofill.
admin-settings-key-login-show-remembered-hint = Show saved-address explanation
admin-settings-help-login-show-remembered-hint = Show explanatory text in the previous-sign-ins dropdown. Hidden by default. Only applies when remembering successful sign-ins is enabled.

admin-settings-key-mail-show-from = Show the composer From field
admin-settings-help-mail-show-from = Show From by default in new composers. Users can reveal it for one message; only authorized addresses can send.
admin-settings-key-accounts-linking-enabled = Allow linked mailbox accounts
admin-settings-help-accounts-linking-enabled = Disabled by default. Global disablement blocks all linked access; both accounts must also satisfy their domain and account policy. Linking requires actual child authentication and fresh primary proof.
admin-settings-key-accounts-use-linked = Use linked mailboxes
admin-settings-help-accounts-use-linked = User opt-out for linked access. Cannot override administrative disablement. Mailbox data is preserved when access is disabled.
admin-settings-key-accounts-max-linked = Maximum linked mailboxes
admin-settings-help-accounts-max-linked = Maximum verified child mailboxes per primary identity, from 1 to 16. Default 5.
admin-settings-key-accounts-store-linked-credentials = Keep linked mailbox access
admin-settings-help-accounts-store-linked-credentials = Keep each linked mailbox's password sealed on the server so its access renews by itself, across sessions and restarts. Never kept for zero-access accounts or mailboxes with two-step verification. Turning it off erases stored passwords; links then renew by signing in again. Default on.

admin-settings-key-privacy-strip-mailer-headers = Remove outgoing mailer headers
admin-settings-help-privacy-strip-mailer-headers = Remove top-level X-Mailer, User-Agent and X-MimeOLE from native SMTP and EWS email. Attached messages and report payloads remain intact. Upstream JMAP proxy sends are not covered.
admin-settings-key-images-trusted-hosts = Trusted image hosts
admin-settings-help-images-trusted-hosts = Up to 100 image hosts, and their subdomains, whose remote images load without a per-message grant when remote content is on ask. Never overrides block mode; a blocked host stays blocked.
admin-settings-key-images-blocked-hosts = Blocked image hosts
admin-settings-help-images-blocked-hosts = Up to 100 image hosts, and their subdomains, whose remote images never load in any mode. Wins over trusted hosts and over any grant.
admin-settings-key-links-trusted-domains = Trusted link domains
admin-settings-help-links-trusted-domains = Up to 100 exact domains whose links open from Review links without the destination step. No wildcards, schemes, ports or IP addresses. Plain-HTTP links are always reviewed. Lock this setting to keep users from changing the list.
admin-settings-key-links-trusted-subdomains = Trust subdomains of trusted link domains
admin-settings-help-links-trusted-subdomains = Off: only the exact domain is trusted. On: names ending in .<domain> are trusted too. Matching is on whole labels, so example.com never trusts evilexample.com.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-rich-text = Rich-text composing
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-rich-text = Whether users may write formatted (HTML) messages. Off sends plain text only.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-attachments = Attachments in new messages
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-attachments = Whether users may attach files to messages they write. Inline images in the body are not counted.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-share-links = Large-file share links
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-share-links = Whether users may send a large file as a Nextcloud share link instead of an attachment.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-scheduled-send = Scheduled send
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-scheduled-send = Whether users may schedule a message to be sent later.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-read-receipts = Request read receipts
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-read-receipts = Whether users may ask recipients for a read receipt.
admin-settings-key-cap-signatures = Signatures
admin-settings-help-cap-signatures = Whether users may create and edit their own signatures.
admin-settings-key-cap-identities = Send-as identities
admin-settings-help-cap-identities = Whether users may add and edit the identities they send as.
admin-settings-key-cap-keys = OpenPGP and S/MIME keys
admin-settings-help-cap-keys = Whether users have the Keys module and may sign and encrypt messages.
admin-settings-key-cap-links-trusted = Edit trusted link domains
admin-settings-help-cap-links-trusted = Whether users may change their own list of trusted link domains. The administrator list still applies.
admin-settings-key-cap-zoom = Reader zoom
admin-settings-help-cap-zoom = Whether users may zoom the message reader.
admin-settings-key-cap-mail-focused-inbox = Focused inbox
admin-settings-help-cap-mail-focused-inbox = Whether users may turn on the Focused and Other inbox tabs.
admin-settings-key-cap-views-events = Events view
admin-settings-help-cap-views-events = Whether users have the Events view of calendar mail.
admin-settings-key-cap-views-attachments = Attachments view
admin-settings-help-cap-views-attachments = Whether users have the Attachments view. The messages stay reachable through search.
admin-settings-key-cap-search-operators = Search operators
admin-settings-help-cap-search-operators = Whether users may search with operators such as from:, subject: or has:attachment.
admin-settings-key-cap-saved-searches = Saved searches
admin-settings-help-cap-saved-searches = Whether users may save searches.
admin-settings-key-cap-vacation = Vacation auto-reply
admin-settings-help-cap-vacation = Whether users may set an automatic vacation reply.
admin-settings-key-cap-labels = Labels
admin-settings-help-cap-labels = Whether users may put labels on messages.
admin-settings-key-cap-snooze = Snooze
admin-settings-help-cap-snooze = Whether users may snooze messages. Ending a snooze stays possible.
admin-settings-key-cap-follow-up = Follow-up reminders
admin-settings-help-cap-follow-up = Whether users may set follow-up reminders on messages. Clearing one stays possible.
admin-settings-key-cap-masked = Masked addresses
admin-settings-help-cap-masked = Whether users may create and manage masked addresses.
admin-settings-key-cap-directory = Directory search
admin-settings-help-cap-directory = Whether users may search the organisation directory.
admin-settings-key-cap-mcp = MCP access
admin-settings-help-cap-mcp = Whether the user's keys and tokens may use the MCP endpoint.
admin-settings-key-cap-appearance-custom = Appearance customisation
admin-settings-help-cap-appearance-custom = Whether users may change their theme, accent, custom and badge colours, density and font. Off keeps the administrator appearance.
admin-settings-key-cap-appearance-custom-code = Custom CSS and scripts
admin-settings-help-cap-appearance-custom-code = Whether users may save their own CSS and appearance scripts. The deployment switches in Appearance still apply above this.
admin-settings-key-cap-avatars = Mailbox avatars
admin-settings-help-cap-avatars = Whether users may change mailbox avatars.
admin-settings-key-cap-shortcuts = Custom keyboard shortcuts
admin-settings-help-cap-shortcuts = Whether users may change keyboard shortcuts. The default shortcuts keep working.
admin-settings-key-cap-analytics = Product analytics
admin-settings-help-cap-analytics = Whether users are asked for analytics consent and may send usage events.
admin-settings-key-cap-apps-native = Desktop and mobile apps
admin-settings-help-cap-apps-native = Whether users may use the desktop and mobile apps.
admin-settings-key-access-protocols = Mail access protocols
admin-settings-help-access-protocols = Which mail server protocols these users may sign in with: imap, pop3, ews. Sign-ins through a JMAP server follow that server.
admin-settings-key-limit-linked-mailboxes = Linked mailboxes per user
admin-settings-help-limit-linked-mailboxes = How many mailboxes a user may link, below the server maximum. 0 means only the server maximum applies.

admin-settings-key-login-show-account-help-notice = Show account-help notice on sign-in
admin-settings-help-login-show-account-help-notice = Show a short explanation after an unsuccessful sign-in. Hidden by default; the notice does not reveal whether an account exists or is disabled.

admin-settings-key-appearance-leetspeak = Leetspeak text style
admin-settings-help-appearance-leetspeak = Display interface labels and read-only message text in leetspeak. Original message and editable text stay unchanged. Users can choose normal text unless this setting is locked.

admin-settings-key-mail-cache-enabled = Enable session cache
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-enabled = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-mailboxes = Cache folder message lists
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-mailboxes = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-messages = Cache opened messages
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-messages = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-fresh-seconds = Freshness interval (seconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-fresh-seconds = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-max-age-seconds = Maximum cached age (seconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-max-age-seconds = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-max-entries = Maximum cached entries
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-max-entries = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-max-bytes = Memory budget (bytes)
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-max-bytes = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-prefetch-enabled = Enable speculative preloading
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-prefetch-enabled = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-hover-enabled = Preload when pointing at a folder
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-hover-enabled = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-focus-enabled = Preload when a folder receives keyboard focus
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-focus-enabled = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-dwell-ms = Pointer and focus delay (milliseconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-dwell-ms = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-idle-enabled = Preload folders while idle
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-idle-enabled = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-idle-delay-ms = Idle delay (milliseconds)
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-idle-delay-ms = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-max-concurrency = Maximum simultaneous preloads
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-max-concurrency = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-max-queued = Maximum queued preloads
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-max-queued = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-preload-messages = Allow speculative message bodies
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-preload-messages = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-excluded-folders = Folders excluded from preloading
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-excluded-folders = Keep recently visited folders and messages in this tab’s memory. Cached content refreshes in the background. Closing the tab or signing out clears it. Preloading never marks mail read or loads remote images.
admin-settings-key-mail-cache-refresh-on-open = Refresh cached content when opening
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-refresh-on-open = Refresh cached content when opening
admin-settings-key-mail-templates-enabled = Response templates
admin-settings-help-mail-templates-enabled = Enable personal and shared plain-text response templates in the composer. Users can opt out unless this setting is locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-templates-allow-personal = Allow personal templates
admin-settings-help-mail-templates-allow-personal = Allow users to create their own response templates. Shared templates are managed separately by administrators.
admin-settings-key-mail-templates-shared = Shared response templates
admin-settings-help-mail-templates-shared = Manage reusable plain-text replies for this scope. Templates never set recipients or send messages.
admin-settings-key-mail-templates-personal = Personal response templates
admin-settings-help-mail-templates-personal = Personal reusable plain-text replies. Creating or editing requires response templates and personal templates to be enabled.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-window = Composer window
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-window = Open new drafts in a workspace tab or separate window. Blocked popups fall back to a tab.
admin-settings-key-mail-reply-copy-to-original = Keep replies in their original folder
admin-settings-help-mail-reply-copy-to-original = Save a sent reply copy in the original message folder where supported.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-check-invalid-recipients = Check for invalid recipients before sending
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-check-invalid-recipients = What happens when a message is sent to an address that is not valid: allow it, warn, warn and remember the choice, or refuse.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-check-missing-attachment = Check for a missing attachment before sending
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-check-missing-attachment = What happens when the text mentions an attachment but none is attached: allow it, warn, warn and remember the choice, or refuse.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-check-empty-subject = Check for an empty subject before sending
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-check-empty-subject = What happens when a message has no subject: allow it, warn, warn and remember the choice, or refuse.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-auto-chip-recipients = Finish typed recipients automatically
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-auto-chip-recipients = Turn a typed address into a recipient chip when a space, comma or semicolon follows it.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-header-collapse = Composer header
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-header-collapse = How the To, Cc, Bcc and Subject rows of the composer behave: expanded, folded to a one-line summary, or auto (folded while writing the body, open when a field is focused). Users can fold or unfold it themselves unless this is locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-header-auto-collapse-seconds = Composer header auto-collapse delay
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-header-auto-collapse-seconds = Seconds the body must hold focus before a complete recipient and subject header folds to its summary. Choose 0 to disable timed folding, or 1–60 seconds. Users can choose unless this is locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-recipient-separator = Recipient separator
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-recipient-separator = The separator inserted after a finished recipient: a comma or a semicolon.
admin-settings-key-mail-reply-from-mode = Identity used for replies and forwards
admin-settings-help-mail-reply-from-mode = Which identity a reply or forward is sent from: the one the original was addressed to, the default, a chooser, or the one currently selected.
admin-settings-key-mail-reply-from-header-priority = Headers that choose the reply identity
admin-settings-help-mail-reply-from-header-priority = The message headers read, in this order, to find the address a message was sent to when choosing the identity for a reply. Names: Delivered-To, X-Original-To, Envelope-To, X-Forwarded-To, Resent-To, To, Cc. A header left out is not read.
admin-settings-key-mail-forward-mode = Default forwarding format
admin-settings-help-mail-forward-mode = Forward inline text or attach the original message as an .eml file.
admin-settings-key-mail-allow-send = Allow sending
admin-settings-help-mail-allow-send = Let users send messages. When off, the composer disables Send and its shortcut and the server refuses submissions; drafts can still be saved.
admin-settings-key-mail-allow-reply = Allow reply
admin-settings-help-mail-allow-reply = Let users reply and reply to all from the reader and with shortcuts. When off, those actions are not offered.
admin-settings-key-mail-allow-forward = Allow forwarding
admin-settings-help-mail-allow-forward = Let users forward messages inline or as an attachment. When off, those actions are not offered.
admin-settings-key-mail-allow-download = Allow downloads
admin-settings-help-mail-allow-download = Let users download messages and attachments. When off, the web app offers no download and the server refuses message export.
admin-settings-key-mail-allow-print = Allow printing
admin-settings-help-mail-allow-print = Let users print a message from the reader. When off, the Print action is not offered.
admin-settings-key-mail-show-spam = Show the Spam folder
admin-settings-help-mail-show-spam = Show the Spam or Junk folder and messages marked as spam. When off they are hidden from the folder list and from search results; nothing is deleted.
admin-settings-key-mail-show-auth-status = Show sender authentication results
admin-settings-help-mail-show-auth-status = Show the SPF, DKIM and DMARC results from the Authentication-Results header in the reader.
admin-settings-key-mail-close-on-delete = Close a message when it is deleted
admin-settings-help-mail-close-on-delete = Close the open message, tab or detached window when that message is deleted or moved to Trash. When off, the reader keeps its previous behaviour.
admin-settings-key-mail-show-go-to-top = Show Go to top button
admin-settings-help-mail-show-go-to-top = Show a Go to top button in the message list that scrolls back to the first message. Off by default.
admin-settings-key-mail-show-create-folder-button = Show Create folder button
admin-settings-help-mail-show-create-folder-button = Show an icon-only Create folder button next to Compose in the sidebar. Off by default.

admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-mode = User-agent observation mode
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-mode = Enforce by default: selected recognized bot headers are blocked immediately when first-request bot blocking is enabled. Observe records decisions without refusal; off disables this dimension. Header claims are not verified identities.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-block-bots = Block recognized bots on the first request
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-block-bots = True by default. Selected search, AI, automation and custom bot headers trigger a temporary HTTP 429 block on the first request in Enforce mode. Observe only records it; false restores the previous request budgets. Missing/uncommon headers, scope and exceptions keep their existing behavior.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-categories = User-agent categories
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-categories = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-weak-requests = Weak-signal request threshold
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-weak-requests = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-crawler-requests = Crawler request threshold
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-crawler-requests = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-window-secs = User-agent observation window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-window-secs = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-max-action = Maximum user-agent response
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-max-action = Maximum escalation for weak or repeated-request evidence, default throttle. This cap does not restrict first-request blocks of selected recognized bot headers.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-scope = User-agent policy scope
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-scope = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-adaptive = Adaptive user-agent observations
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-adaptive = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-patterns = User-agent patterns
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-patterns = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-security-protection-user-agent-exceptions = User-agent exceptions
admin-settings-help-security-protection-user-agent-exceptions = Configures this part of optional user-agent observation. Client-provided user-agent text is a weak signal, not proof of identity or abuse.
admin-settings-key-mail-reader-unsafe-html-mode = Potentially unsafe message HTML
admin-settings-help-mail-reader-unsafe-html-mode = Ask offers a per-message sanitized HTML button by default. Strict shows only safe text; sanitized shows cleaned HTML automatically. Active content and automatic remote resources remain blocked. Lock to enforce this policy.
admin-settings-key-reader-attachments-density = Attachment density
admin-settings-help-reader-attachments-density = Compact file buttons by default, or comfortable previews. This controls presentation when a message's attachments are expanded.
admin-settings-key-cap-compose-open-tracking = Allow message open tracking
admin-settings-help-cap-compose-open-tracking = Whether this account may record message opens. Requires a configured public URL; disabled accounts cannot create or bind tracking tokens.
admin-settings-key-mail-open-tracking = Track opens by default
admin-settings-help-mail-open-tracking = Default per-message tracking choice for eligible formatted messages. Users can override it unless locked; disabling the tracking capability always takes precedence.
admin-settings-key-cap-reading-original-html = Allow Original HTML capability
admin-settings-help-cap-reading-original-html = Permit users to enable the Original HTML option for individual messages. Also enable Original HTML view in their feature profile. Scripts and forms remain disabled; remote resources still use privacy controls and the proxy.
admin-settings-key-mail-reader-allow-original-html = Offer Original HTML per message
admin-settings-help-mail-reader-allow-original-html = Show the explicit Show Original HTML option in the reader. This keeps original formatting without selecting it automatically. Requires the Original HTML capability and feature profile; locked strict HTML handling and plain-text-only mode still take precedence.
admin-settings-key-privacy-tracker-override-allowed = Offer per-message tracker consent
admin-settings-help-privacy-tracker-override-allowed = Show the Allow trackers action in the message privacy bar. Available by default, but never active without an explicit grant. A locked tracker-blocking policy still forbids the override.
admin-settings-key-privacy-max-concurrent-global = Global parallel image fetches
admin-settings-help-privacy-max-concurrent-global = Maximum active image network requests across this server process. Range 1–256; default 128. Message and account limits still apply.
admin-settings-key-privacy-max-concurrent-pipeline = Concurrent image processing pipelines
admin-settings-help-privacy-max-concurrent-pipeline = Maximum images admitted to fetch, decode and cache publication together. Range 1–256; default 128. Network and decoder ceilings are enforced separately.
admin-settings-key-privacy-max-concurrent-decodes = Parallel image decoders
admin-settings-help-privacy-max-concurrent-decodes = Maximum image decodes running at once. Range 1–16; default 10. Higher values use more CPU and memory.
admin-settings-key-privacy-max-queued-requests = Waiting image requests
admin-settings-help-privacy-max-queued-requests = Maximum requests waiting for image network or processing capacity. Range 16–16384; default 2048. Overflow or queue expiry remains retryable.
admin-settings-key-privacy-rate-burst = Image request burst allowance
admin-settings-help-privacy-rate-burst = Initial and maximum per-account fetch tokens, replenished at the configured image request rate. Range 1–12000; default 1024. Cached successes do not consume tokens.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-rate-mode = Image request rate sizing
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-rate-mode = Automatic scales per-account burst and refill from replica capacity, queue load and the message's image count within the floors and ceilings below. Manual uses the burst allowance and request rate settings exactly. Default automatic. Requests over the allowance wait for a token until the fetch queue deadline; authentication and grants are checked first.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-rate-burst-floor = Automatic burst allowance floor
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-rate-burst-floor = Lowest per-account burst allowance in automatic rate mode. Range 1–12000; default 64.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-rate-burst-ceiling = Automatic burst allowance ceiling
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-rate-burst-ceiling = Highest per-account burst allowance in automatic rate mode. Range 1–12000; default 2048.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-rate-refill-floor = Automatic refill floor
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-rate-refill-floor = Lowest per-account refill, in fetch tokens per minute, in automatic rate mode. Range 10–60000; default 300.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-rate-refill-ceiling = Automatic refill ceiling
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-rate-refill-ceiling = Highest per-account refill, in fetch tokens per minute, in automatic rate mode. Range 10–60000; default 6000.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-mode = Image cache sizing
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-mode = Automatic sizes the cache from the memory left after decoder and pipeline reservations and lengthens the lifetime while the hit rate is high and memory is free. Manual uses the cache size, entry count and lifetime settings exactly. Default automatic.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-bytes-floor = Automatic cache size floor
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-bytes-floor = Smallest image cache in bytes in automatic mode. Range 0–1073741824; default 16777216.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-bytes-ceiling = Automatic cache size ceiling
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-bytes-ceiling = Largest image cache in bytes in automatic mode. Range 0–1073741824; default 268435456.
admin-settings-key-privacy-cache-entries = Image cache entry limit
admin-settings-help-privacy-cache-entries = Most cached images; the fixed count in manual mode and the ceiling in automatic mode. Range 16–65536; default 4096.
admin-settings-key-privacy-cache-entry-bytes = Largest cached image
admin-settings-help-privacy-cache-entry-bytes = Largest single re-encoded image kept in the cache, in bytes. Larger images are served but not kept. Range 65536–16777216; default 4194304.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-ttl-floor-secs = Automatic cache lifetime floor
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-ttl-floor-secs = Shortest cache lifetime in seconds in automatic mode, used on a low hit rate or under memory pressure. Range 0–86400; default 300.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-ttl-ceiling-secs = Automatic cache lifetime ceiling
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-ttl-ceiling-secs = Longest cache lifetime in seconds in automatic mode, used on a high hit rate with free memory. Range 0–86400; default 21600.
admin-settings-key-privacy-cache-ttl-secs = Successful image cache lifetime
admin-settings-help-privacy-cache-ttl-secs = Seconds decoded images remain reusable in this process. Range 0–86400; default 3600. Zero disables successful-image reuse; authorization is always checked first.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-latency-tracking = Image proxy speed tracking
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-latency-tracking = Records how long each proxied image takes (median, p95, p99 and the time spent waiting, fetching and decoding) as counts in fixed time buckets in memory. No URLs, hosts or accounts are stored. On by default; the history resets on restart and is per server process. Turning it off stops new recording; the Speed section keeps showing what was recorded.
admin-settings-key-privacy-negative-cache-ttl-secs = Failed image cache lifetime
admin-settings-help-privacy-negative-cache-ttl-secs = Seconds eligible upstream failures are remembered to avoid repeated requests. Range 0–300; default 10. Zero disables failure reuse. Explicit retry clears the affected failures.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-retry-attempts = Automatic image retries
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-retry-attempts = Maximum retries for temporary image failures in one visible message load. Range 0–8; default 3. Zero disables automatic retries while preserving manual retry.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-retry-delay-ms = Automatic image retry delay
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-retry-delay-ms = Milliseconds between automatic image retries, after the current frame settles. Range 500–60000; default 5000. Permanent refusals are not retried automatically.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-decode-timeout-ms = Image decode timeout
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-decode-timeout-ms = Wall-clock milliseconds allowed for one sandboxed image decode after its fetch. Range 1000–60000; default 10000. Increase for large images; network timeouts remain separate.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-concurrency-mode = Image concurrency profile
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-concurrency-mode = Automatic adapts to CPU capacity, container memory and each message's approved image count. Low resource, Balanced and High throughput also adapt with different safety caps. Manual uses the numeric ceilings directly. Applying a profile changes only this setting.
admin-settings-key-links-trusted-senders = Trusted link senders
admin-settings-help-links-trusted-senders = Exact sender mailboxes whose reviewed message links may open without per-message consent. One address per entry.
admin-settings-key-appearance-font-size = Interface font size
admin-settings-help-appearance-font-size = Interface font size in pixels, from 12 to 24.
admin-settings-key-appearance-font-weight = Interface font weight
admin-settings-help-appearance-font-weight = Base weight of interface text: 300, 400, 500 or 600. Emphasized text keeps its hierarchy.
admin-settings-key-appearance-font-color = Interface text colour
admin-settings-help-appearance-font-color = Interface text colour as #RRGGBB. Leave empty to follow the theme.
admin-settings-key-appearance-low-contrast = Soften text contrast
admin-settings-help-appearance-low-contrast = Soften the contrast of interface text.
admin-settings-key-mail-message-list-order = Message list order
admin-settings-help-mail-message-list-order = Sort messages by received or sent date, sender, subject, importance, or size, in either direction. With grouping enabled, this orders messages within each group.
admin-settings-key-mail-list-page-size = Message list page size
admin-settings-help-mail-list-page-size = How many messages the list fetches each time a user scrolls to the end. Default 50, from 20 to 200. Users choose their own value unless you lock this.
admin-settings-key-mail-message-list-style = Message list style
admin-settings-help-mail-message-list-style = Show the message list as cards or as rows with column headings.
admin-settings-key-mail-message-list-preview = Message list previews
admin-settings-help-mail-message-list-preview = Show body snippets in the message list.
admin-settings-key-mail-after-delete = After deleting a message
admin-settings-help-mail-after-delete = Which message the reader shows after the open message is deleted: next, previous or none.
admin-settings-key-reader-attachments-at-end = Attachments after the body
admin-settings-help-reader-attachments-at-end = Show attachments after the message body instead of before it.
admin-settings-key-notifications-ask-permission = Offer notification permission
admin-settings-help-notifications-ask-permission = Offer the browser notification permission prompt to users on devices that have not allowed or blocked notifications.

# Image proxy cache tiers.
admin-settings-cat-image-proxy = Image proxy
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-ram-max-mi-b = RAM tier maximum
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-ram-max-mi-b = Upper bound in MiB for the in-memory image tier, applied on top of the automatic or manual cache size. Zero adds no cap. Keep it small and let the disk tier hold the bulk. Range 0–1048576; default 0.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-enabled = Image disk tier
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-enabled = Keeps already re-encoded images on disk behind the RAM tier. Off by default; when the directory is missing, full or read-only the cache silently continues in RAM only. Only jail output is stored, under hashed file names.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-path = Image disk directory
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-path = Absolute directory used for the disk tier. Empty uses an image-cache folder beside the database file. Mount a writable volume there when the root filesystem is read-only. Relative paths and .. are refused and leave the tier off.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-mode = Image disk sizing
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-mode = Automatic uses a tenth of the space this cache could use (free space plus what it already holds), between the floor and ceiling and never more than half of that space. Manual uses the maximum size below exactly. Default automatic.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-max-mi-b = Image disk size (manual)
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-max-mi-b = Disk tier size in MiB in manual mode; the readout shows the effective size either way. Range 1–1048576; default 512.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-floor-mi-b = Automatic disk size floor
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-floor-mi-b = Smallest disk tier in MiB in automatic mode; also used while free space is unknown. Range 0–1048576; default 64.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-ceiling-mi-b = Automatic disk size ceiling
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-ceiling-mi-b = Largest disk tier in MiB in automatic mode. Range 0–1048576; default 4096.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-entries = Disk entry limit
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-entries = Most images kept on disk. Each entry also costs a fixed amount of RAM in the index, which counts against the RAM tier. Range 16–1048576; default 16384.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-entry-bytes = Largest disk image
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-entry-bytes = Largest single re-encoded image written to disk, in bytes. Images above the RAM entry limit but within this one go straight to disk. Range 65536–67108864; default 8388608.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-min-hits = Hits before a disk write
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-min-hits = Hits a RAM entry needs before its eviction writes it to disk instead of dropping it. Zero writes every evicted entry whose score passes the demote threshold. Range 0–100; default 1.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-disk-write-queue-mi-b = Disk write queue
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-disk-write-queue-mi-b = Image data in MiB that may wait for the background disk writer. It counts against the RAM tier; past it, evicted images are dropped instead of queued. Range 1–256; default 8.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-ttl-step-secs = Lifetime step per hit
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-ttl-step-secs = Seconds added to an image's remaining lifetime on a hit, multiplied by 1 plus the log of its decayed hit count, so frequently used images live longer. Zero keeps every image at the base lifetime. Range 0–86400; default 600.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-ttl-max-secs = Longest extended lifetime
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-ttl-max-secs = Longest remaining lifetime in seconds that hits can build up. Range 60–2592000; default 86400.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-max-age-secs = Image maximum age
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-max-age-secs = Age in seconds after which an image is fetched again whatever its hits. The fetch path keeps no upstream ETag or Last-Modified, so there is no conditional revalidation; the image is simply refetched. Range 3600–7776000; default 604800.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-score-half-life-secs = Score half-life
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-score-half-life-secs = Seconds for an image's hit count and recency to halve in the priority score that decides RAM, disk and eviction. Range 60–604800; default 3600.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-score-demote-milli = Demote score
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-score-demote-milli = Score, in thousandths, below which a RAM image is demoted to disk or dropped. The promote threshold is this plus the hysteresis. Range 0–10000; default 300.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-score-hysteresis-percent = Promote hysteresis
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-score-hysteresis-percent = Percentage by which the promote threshold sits above the demote threshold. A score between the two keeps the image where it is. Range 0–500; default 50.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-context-open-percent = Open message weight
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-context-open-percent = Score weight in percent for images requested for a message. A message's images count as Recent after ten idle minutes. Range 100–1000; default 200.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-context-recent-percent = Recent message weight
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-context-recent-percent = Score weight in percent for recently used images. Requests that name no message weigh 100. Range 100–1000; default 150.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-account-share-percent = Account RAM share
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-account-share-percent = Largest share of the RAM tier one account's inserts may fill while other accounts use the cache; beyond it the account evicts its own lowest-scoring images first. A single account may use all of it. Range 1–100; default 50.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-sweep-secs = Cache sweep interval
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-sweep-secs = Seconds between background sweeps that expire images, rescore a bounded batch, demote cold RAM images under pressure and re-check free disk space. Range 5–3600; default 30.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-snapshot-secs = Index snapshot interval
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-snapshot-secs = Seconds between atomic snapshots of the disk index, which keep hit counts and extended lifetimes across restarts without a write per hit. Zero turns snapshots off; a restart then reads each file's header. Range 0–86400; default 300.
admin-settings-key-privacy-image-sweep-batch = Sweep batch size
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-sweep-batch = Entries one maintenance sweep may expire, rescore or evict. Bounds the work done under the cache lock. Range 16–8192; default 256.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-stale-secs = Serve stale while revalidating (seconds)
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-stale-secs = Seconds past its freshness a cached image is still served at once while it is revalidated in the background. Zero turns it off. Range 0–86400; default 3600.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-cache-max-stale-secs = Keep stale when the origin fails (seconds)
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-cache-max-stale-secs = Seconds past its freshness a cached image is kept to answer when the origin cannot be reached. Never below the revalidation window. Range 0–604800; default 86400.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-resize-enabled = Resize large images
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-resize-enabled = Scale oversized remote images down to the width the reader asks for (320, 640, 960, 1280 or 1600 pixels). Animated images are served unscaled. Off by default.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-resize-max-width = Widest resized image (pixels)
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-resize-max-width = The widest image the resize produces. Range 320–1600; default 1600.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-resize-max-pixels = Largest image to resize (pixels)
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-resize-max-pixels = Images with more decoded pixels than this are served unscaled; the size is read from the header before any decoding. Range 100000–64000000; default 4000000.

admin-settings-key-privacy-image-resize-format = Resized image format
admin-settings-help-privacy-image-resize-format = Auto picks the best encoder in the build, which is PNG. Default auto.

admin-image-proxy-title = Image cache readout
admin-image-proxy-unavailable = The image cache readout is not available.
admin-image-proxy-unknown = unknown
admin-image-proxy-ram = RAM tier: { $used } used of { $budget } (configured { $configured }), { $entries } images, { $hot } hot, { $cold } cold, hit rate { $hit }.
admin-image-proxy-disk-off = Disk tier: off.
admin-image-proxy-disk = Disk tier: { $bytes } used of an effective { $budget } ({ $mode }; floor { $floor }, ceiling { $ceiling }, manual { $manual }), { $entries } images, { $hot } hot, { $cold } cold, hit rate { $hit }.
admin-image-proxy-disk-inactive = Disk tier: on but not active. { $reason }
admin-image-proxy-moves = Promotions per minute: { $perMin }. Total promotions { $promotions }, demotions { $demotions }, drops { $drops }. Index entries: { $index }.
admin-image-proxy-refresh = Refresh readout
admin-settings-key-security-trust-enabled = Trust tiers
admin-settings-help-security-trust-enabled = Give each request a tier: signed in, known source (a recent successful sign-in from that address) or unknown. Only anonymous request allowances change; credentials, second factors and lockouts are never relaxed.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-known-ttl-days = Known source window (days)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-known-ttl-days = How long a successful sign-in keeps its address known. Failed attempts never count.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-known-capacity = Known sources kept
admin-settings-help-security-trust-known-capacity = Most known sources kept in memory (a salted hash, a country and an account count each). The oldest is dropped first.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-persist = Save known sources across restarts
admin-settings-help-security-trust-persist = Save the known-source table (keyed hashes, country, last-seen time, account count) to the settings store and load it at startup. Entries older than the window are dropped.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-persist-interval-secs = Known-source save interval (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-persist-interval-secs = Seconds between saves, 30 to 3600. A save happens only when the table changed, and once more at graceful shutdown.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-unknown-percent = Unknown source allowance (%)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-unknown-percent = Anonymous request allowance of an unknown source as a percentage of the configured limits. 100 keeps the baseline; lower is stricter.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-known-percent = Known source allowance (%)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-known-percent = Anonymous request allowance of a known source. 200 doubles request budgets and halves the sign-in cooldown and challenge difficulty. Never bypasses credentials, second factors or lockouts.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-missing = Bots: empty user-agent
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-missing = Action for anonymous requests with an empty user-agent: allow, limit or block. Signed-in sessions are never affected.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-uncommon = Bots: unrecognised user-agent
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-uncommon = Action for anonymous requests with an unrecognised user-agent: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-automation = Bots: scripts and automation
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-automation = Action for anonymous requests claiming a script, HTTP library, headless browser or generic bot: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-search = Bots: search crawlers
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-search = Action for anonymous requests claiming a search-engine crawler: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-ai-training = Bots: AI training crawlers
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-ai-training = Action for anonymous requests claiming GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Amazonbot, Bytespider, Google-Extended or Applebot-Extended: allow, limit or block. A claim is a header, not verified identity.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-ai-search = Bots: AI search crawlers
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-ai-search = Action for anonymous requests claiming OAI-SearchBot, PerplexityBot or Claude-SearchBot: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-ai-user = Bots: AI user fetchers
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-ai-user = Action for anonymous requests claiming ChatGPT-User or Claude-User: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-ua-custom = Bots: custom patterns
admin-settings-help-security-trust-ua-custom = Action for anonymous requests matching the custom user-agent patterns: allow, limit or block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-enabled = Block admin discovery from unknown countries
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-enabled = Block a source that probes for the admin console from a country with no recent successful sign-in. Needs a readable country database and admin-probe protection. MW_ADMIN_GEO_ENABLED=false turns it off for recovery.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-countries = Always-known countries (admin block)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-countries = Uppercase ISO country codes always treated as known, besides the countries of recent successful sign-ins.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-lookup-failure = Source with no country
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-lookup-failure = allow does not block and logs the case; unknown treats a source with no detected country as an unknown country.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-threshold = Probes before a block
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-threshold = Admin-discovery probes from an unknown country inside the window that start a block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-window-secs = Probe window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-window-secs = Window for the probe threshold.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-block-on-first = Block on the first probe
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-block-on-first = Block on the first probe from an unknown country. Raises the chance of locking out a travelling administrator.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-block-secs = First block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-block-secs = Length of the first block.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-second-block-secs = Second block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-second-block-secs = Length of the second block of the same source inside the repeat period.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-max-block-secs = Repeat block (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-max-block-secs = Length of the third and every later block inside the repeat period.
admin-settings-key-security-trust-admin-geo-repeat-days = Repeat period (days)
admin-settings-help-security-trust-admin-geo-repeat-days = A block within this many days of the previous one counts as a repeat and uses the next, longer length.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-mode = Per-account sign-in country policy
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-mode = Off by default. Block sign-ins from countries the account has not used before, or from any country outside its allowed list. Allowlisted IPs and countries always pass. Applies to new webmail sign-ins only, never to existing sessions or protocol clients. Country detection uses an IP geolocation database that can be wrong or out of date; VPNs, mobile carriers, proxies and travel can block a legitimate sign-in or let a foreign one through. Add trusted IPs or countries to the allowlist.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-allow-countries = Account allowed countries
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-allow-countries = Uppercase ISO country codes always allowed for the account. Country detection uses an IP geolocation database that can be wrong or out of date; VPNs, mobile carriers, proxies and travel can block a legitimate sign-in or let a foreign one through. Add trusted IPs or countries to the allowlist.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-allow-ips = Account allowed IPs
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-allow-ips = IP addresses or CIDR networks always allowed for the account. A single IPv6 address means its /64.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-global-allow-countries = Allowed countries for every account
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-global-allow-countries = Uppercase ISO country codes allowed for every account, added to each account's own list.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-global-allow-ips = Allowed IPs for every account
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-global-allow-ips = IP addresses or CIDR networks (an office or VPN) allowed for every account, added to each account's own list.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-lookup-failure = Source with no country (account policy)
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-lookup-failure = When the source has no detected country: allow the sign-in and log it, or deny it.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-account-geo-history-days = Account country history (days)
admin-settings-help-security-signin-account-geo-history-days = How many days a country stays in an account's own sign-in history for the unusual-countries policy. It is kept apart from the authentication log, so shortening the log does not shorten it.
admin-settings-key-security-geo-no-database = No country database: default behaviour
admin-settings-help-security-geo-no-database = What country features do when no database is loaded: allow, treat the source as an unknown country, or block (block applies to sign-ins only). A feature's own setting also applies and the stricter one wins.
admin-settings-key-security-geo-not-found = Address not in the database: default behaviour
admin-settings-help-security-geo-not-found = What country features do when a database is loaded but has no entry for the address. Private, loopback and link-local addresses are local networks and are never affected.
admin-settings-key-security-signin-geo-no-database = Instance sign-in policy without a database
admin-settings-help-security-signin-geo-no-database = When the instance sign-in country policy is on and no database is loaded: block sign-ins (fail closed) or allow them unchecked. Local networks are always allowed.
admin-settings-key-security-geo-session-lookup-failure = Session alerts without a country
admin-settings-help-security-geo-session-lookup-failure = When a signed-in request's country cannot be determined: ignore it, or raise one session alert per session per day. It never blocks or revokes a session.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-framing-mode = Protocol guard: request framing
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-framing-mode = Request-smuggling class: Content-Length together with Transfer-Encoding, Transfer-Encoding other than exactly chunked (or on HTTP/1.0 and HTTP/2), non-numeric or conflicting Content-Length. Enforce answers 400 and closes the connection; detect only counts. A route-prefix exemption never applies to this class.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-host-mode = Protocol guard: Host syntax
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-host-mode = Host header syntax: missing on HTTP/1.1, empty, repeated, or holding userinfo, whitespace or path characters. IPv6 literals, ports and a trailing dot are accepted. Enforce answers 400 and closes the connection.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-host-pinning-mode = Protocol guard: Host must match the public name
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-host-pinning-mode = Host not matching the host of MW_PUBLIC_URL or one of allowedHosts. Does nothing while neither names a host. Detect by default because proxies and health checks may send an internal name.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-path-control-mode = Protocol guard: control characters in the path
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-path-control-mode = NUL, control characters or encoded CR/LF (%00, %0d, %0a) in the request path. Enforce answers 400. Never exempted by a route prefix.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-target-mode = Protocol guard: request-target tricks
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-target-mode = Double or overlong percent-encoding of dots and slashes, encoded dots, dot segments, empty path segments (//), backslashes, raw non-ASCII bytes, and an absolute-form target naming another authority than Host.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-path-length-mode = Protocol guard: path and query length
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-path-length-mode = Path or query longer than maxPathBytes or maxQueryBytes. Enforce answers 414.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-method-mode = Protocol guard: HTTP methods
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-method-mode = Method outside allowedMethods (TRACE, TRACK, CONNECT and unknown or lower-case methods by default). Enforce answers 405.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-duplicate-headers-mode = Protocol guard: repeated single-value headers
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-duplicate-headers-mode = A header that should appear once appearing more than once (Content-Type, Authorization, Origin, Referer, User-Agent, Sec-Fetch-*, conditional and range headers), a repeated Content-Length with equal values, or repeated Cookie headers on HTTP/1.x.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-forwarded-mode = Protocol guard: forwarding headers from untrusted peers
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-forwarded-mode = Forwarded, X-Forwarded-* or X-Real-IP sent by a peer outside MW_TRUSTED_PROXIES. The headers are never trusted either way; this records the attempt. It counts toward adaptive protection only when trusted proxies are configured.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-header-hygiene-mode = Protocol guard: header hygiene
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-header-hygiene-mode = Header count, a single value, or the Cookie header over the configured caps; non-ASCII header bytes; Upgrade or Connection: upgrade outside the WebSocket route; Connection naming headers such as Content-Length or Host. Enforce answers 431 for size and count findings and 400 for the rest.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-body-mode = Protocol guard: request body framing
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-body-mode = GET or HEAD carrying a body, Content-Length above maxBodyBytes (413), Expect other than 100-continue (417) or without a body.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-path-bytes = Protocol guard: longest path (bytes)
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-path-bytes = Longest request path before the path-length class reports it.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-query-bytes = Protocol guard: longest query (bytes)
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-query-bytes = Longest query string before the path-length class reports it.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-header-count = Protocol guard: most headers
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-header-count = Most header fields in one request before the header-hygiene class reports it. The listener's own hard limit (MW_HTTP_MAX_HEADERS) still applies.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-header-value-bytes = Protocol guard: longest header value (bytes)
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-header-value-bytes = Longest single header value before the header-hygiene class reports it.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-cookie-bytes = Protocol guard: largest Cookie header (bytes)
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-cookie-bytes = Combined size of Cookie headers before the header-hygiene class reports it.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-max-body-bytes = Protocol guard: largest declared body (bytes)
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-max-body-bytes = Largest Content-Length the body class accepts without reporting it. Keep it above the largest upload or import a route accepts; a route-prefix exemption can raise it for one route.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-allowed-methods = Protocol guard: allowed methods
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-allowed-methods = Methods the method class accepts. The default lists the ordinary HTTP verbs and the WebDAV, CalDAV and CardDAV verbs; the server mounts no inbound DAV routes today, so those reach a 405 at the router.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-allowed-hosts = Protocol guard: extra accepted hosts
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-allowed-hosts = Host names accepted by the host-pinning class in addition to the host of MW_PUBLIC_URL, for example an internal name a proxy or health check uses. Ports and a trailing dot are ignored.
admin-settings-key-security-protocol-exempt-prefixes = Protocol guard: exempt route prefixes
admin-settings-help-security-protocol-exempt-prefixes = Route prefixes (each starting with / and longer than one character) for which the heuristic classes do not run, for a legitimate client that needs it, for example a large upload route. Matches whole path segments. Framing and path-control findings are never exempted, and / is ignored.
admin-settings-key-security-health-mode = Health endpoint access
admin-settings-help-security-health-mode = Who may reach /healthz and /readyz. internal-only: loopback, private, link-local and unique-local client addresses. allowlist: those plus the networks below. open: anyone. Anyone else gets the same 404 as an unknown path. A request with the MW_HEALTH_TOKEN token is always admitted. The client address is the trusted-proxy-resolved one: behind a reverse proxy without MW_FORWARDED_MODE and MW_TRUSTED_PROXIES every request looks like the proxy's private address, so the whole internet is admitted.
admin-settings-key-security-health-networks = Health endpoint networks
admin-settings-help-security-health-networks = IP addresses or CIDR networks that may reach /healthz and /readyz in allowlist mode, in addition to the internal ranges, for example an external uptime monitor.

admin-settings-key-security-spray-enabled = Password spray detection
admin-settings-help-security-spray-enabled = Counts the distinct usernames one source fails with. Only a keyed hash of each username is kept, in memory.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-window-secs = Spray window (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-spray-window-secs = Window in which one source's failed sign-ins are counted by distinct username. Default 900.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-challenge-at = Spray: challenge threshold
admin-settings-help-security-spray-challenge-at = Distinct failing usernames from one source inside the window that force the proof-of-work challenge for that source. Successful sign-ins never count, so a shared office or campus address is not affected. Default 10.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-pace-at = Spray: pacing threshold
admin-settings-help-security-spray-pace-at = Distinct failing usernames that add extra waiting between attempts from the source. Default 15.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-lock-at = Spray: lock threshold
admin-settings-help-security-spray-lock-at = Distinct failing usernames that lock the source for the lock length, through the existing sign-in lock. Default 25.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-pace-secs = Spray: pacing wait (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-spray-pace-secs = Seconds between attempts from a source at or above the pacing threshold. Default 10.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-lock-secs = Spray: lock length (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-spray-lock-secs = Length of the temporary lock. An administrator unlocking the source also resets its count. Default 900.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-known-multiplier = Spray: known-source multiplier
admin-settings-help-security-spray-known-multiplier = Multiplier on the three thresholds for a known source, one with a recent successful sign-in. Default 3.
admin-settings-key-security-spray-capacity = Spray: tracked sources
admin-settings-help-security-spray-capacity = Most sources tracked in memory; the least recently active are dropped first. Default 20000.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-enabled = Instance-wide spike detection
admin-settings-help-security-spike-enabled = Learns a baseline of failed sign-ins and enters heightened mode when the whole instance is far above it. It never locks the instance.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-multiplier-percent = Spike: multiplier (%)
admin-settings-help-security-spike-multiplier-percent = A signal counts when it is at least this percentage of its learned baseline (400 = four times) and above its absolute floor.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-min-failures-per-min = Spike: minimum failures per minute
admin-settings-help-security-spike-min-failures-per-min = Floor: failed sign-ins per minute below which the failure-rate signal never counts. Default 20.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-min-sources = Spike: minimum failing sources
admin-settings-help-security-spike-min-sources = Floor: distinct failing sources in a five-minute bucket below which that signal never counts. Default 10.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-min-usernames = Spike: minimum failing usernames
admin-settings-help-security-spike-min-usernames = Floor: distinct failing usernames in a five-minute bucket below which that signal never counts. Default 30.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-signals-required = Spike: signals required
admin-settings-help-security-spike-signals-required = Signals that must be over their baseline and floor together. The distributed-spray signature counts as two. Default 2.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-warmup-hours = Spike: warm-up (hours)
admin-settings-help-security-spike-warmup-hours = Hours of observed traffic before heightened mode can start. Until then the baseline only learns. Default 48.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-adapt-hours = Spike: baseline adaptation (hours)
admin-settings-help-security-spike-adapt-hours = Time constant of the baseline. Longer absorbs growth more slowly. A spike never updates the baseline. Default 168.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-duration-secs = Spike: heightened mode length (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-spike-duration-secs = How long heightened mode lasts after the last evidence of a spike; it is extended while signals stay above half their trigger level. Default 1800.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-force-challenge = Spike: force challenge
admin-settings-help-security-spike-force-challenge = In heightened mode, require the proof-of-work challenge for anonymous sign-ins from unknown sources. Authenticated users and known sources are unaffected.
admin-settings-key-security-spike-pace-factor-percent = Spike: sign-in wait (%)
admin-settings-help-security-spike-pace-factor-percent = In heightened mode, the sign-in wait for unknown sources as a percentage of the usual wait. Default 300.
admin-settings-key-security-session-binding-enabled = Session binding
admin-settings-help-security-session-binding-enabled = Binds each browser session to keyed hashes of its client attributes. Native clients with a bearer token, API keys and protocol clients are exempt.
admin-settings-key-security-session-binding-attributes = Session binding: attributes
admin-settings-help-security-session-binding-attributes = Attributes bound: browser, os, hints, language, country, network (IPv4 /16, IPv6 /48). Network is off by default because mobile networks move. Unknown names are ignored.
admin-settings-key-security-session-binding-strictness = Session binding: strictness
admin-settings-help-security-session-binding-strictness = Tolerant accepts browser updates and a single soft attribute change; strict flags any soft difference.
admin-settings-key-security-session-binding-webmail-action = Session binding: webmail action
admin-settings-help-security-session-binding-webmail-action = What a webmail session mismatch does: off, detect (record only), step-up (ask for password and second factor again) or revoke the session. Default step-up.
admin-settings-key-security-session-binding-admin-action = Session binding: admin console action
admin-settings-help-security-session-binding-admin-action = What an admin console session mismatch does: off, detect, step-up or revoke. Default revoke.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-enabled = Session theft detection
admin-settings-help-security-theft-enabled = Detects reuse of a rotated session id, impossible travel and concurrent use from different countries.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-rotation-grace-secs = Theft: rotation grace (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-theft-rotation-grace-secs = After a session rotates, the old id may be presented again for this long (an in-flight request) before it counts as theft. Default 30.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-min-travel-secs = Theft: minimum travel time (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-theft-min-travel-secs = A country change sooner than this after the previous request is treated as impossible travel. Country detection may be inaccurate; VPNs and mobile networks can cause false changes. Default 3600.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-concurrent-use = Theft: concurrent use
admin-settings-help-security-theft-concurrent-use = Flags one session used alternately from different countries (or networks) within five minutes: off, country or network. Country detection may be inaccurate; VPNs and mobile networks can cause false changes.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-webmail-action = Theft: webmail response
admin-settings-help-security-theft-webmail-action = Response to impossible travel or concurrent use on a webmail session: alert, step-up or revoke. Reuse of a rotated session always revokes. Default step-up.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-admin-action = Theft: admin console response
admin-settings-help-security-theft-admin-action = Response to impossible travel or concurrent use on an admin console session: alert, step-up or revoke. Default revoke.
admin-settings-key-security-theft-retention-days = Theft: record retention (days)
admin-settings-help-security-theft-retention-days = How long rotated-session markers and per-session security records are kept; set it at least as long as the longest session lifetime. Default 15.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-country-change = Country-change alert
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-country-change = Warns when a signed-in session is used from a country it was not started in. Country detection may be inaccurate; VPNs and mobile networks can cause false changes. Users can change this unless it is locked; a user turning it off is honoured only if muting is allowed.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-country-change-enabled = Country-change alert: global switch
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-country-change-enabled = Off disables the country-change alert for everyone. Country detection may be inaccurate; VPNs and mobile networks can cause false changes.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-country-change-cooldown-secs = Country-change alert: cooldown (seconds)
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-country-change-cooldown-secs = Minimum time between country-change alerts of one session. Each new country alerts once per session. Default 300.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-country-change-user-mute = Country-change alert: allow users to mute
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-country-change-user-mute = Whether a user may turn their own country-change alert off. When off, the server keeps alerting even if the user's own setting is off.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-channels = Security alert channels
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-channels = How session security warnings reach the user: in the app, as a message in their own mailbox, or both. Users can change this unless it is locked.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-email-enabled = Security alerts by email
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-email-enabled = Allows session security warnings to be delivered into the user's own mailbox. No message is sent over SMTP; without a delivery session the warning stays in the app and the audit log.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-sensitivity = Security alert sensitivity
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-sensitivity = Low only warns on location findings and never steps up or revokes; normal follows the administrator's actions; high doubles the travel interval and also checks concurrent networks. Users can change this unless it is locked.
admin-settings-key-security-alerts-notice-retention-days = Security notices: retention (days)
admin-settings-help-security-alerts-notice-retention-days = How long in-app security notices are kept per account (at most 20 per account). Default 30.

