admin-settings-inline-effective = In effect:
admin-settings-inline-reset = Discard changes
admin-settings-inline-domains = Per-domain values
admin-attachments-tab-lists = Allow and block lists
admin-attachments-tab-limits = Limits
admin-attachments-tab-delivery = Download and preview
admin-attachments-tab-warnings = Warnings
admin-attachments-tab-test = Test a file
admin-attachments-tab-denied = You do not have access to this tab.
admin-attachments-group-lists = Allow and block lists
admin-attachments-group-limits = Size limit
admin-attachments-group-delivery = Download and preview
admin-attachments-group-warnings = Warnings
admin-attachments-add-extension = Extension, for example pdf or .tar.gz
admin-attachments-add-mime = MIME type, for example image/png or image/*
admin-attachments-add = Add
admin-attachments-remove = Remove { $rule }
admin-attachments-filter = Filter the list
admin-attachments-list-label = Rules in this list
admin-attachments-count = { $count } of { $max } rules
admin-attachments-empty-list = No rules in this list.
admin-attachments-none-match = No rule matches the filter.
admin-attachments-bulk = Paste many
admin-attachments-bulk-add = Add all
admin-attachments-import = Import a text file
admin-attachments-export = Export as text
admin-attachments-err-extension = Not an extension. Use letters, digits, dashes and underscores, up to 32 characters; dots may separate parts, as in tar.gz.
admin-attachments-err-mime = Not a MIME type. Use type/subtype, or type/* for every subtype.
admin-attachments-err-long = That rule is too long.
admin-attachments-invalid = Not added, not a valid rule: { $entries }
admin-attachments-duplicates = Already in the list: { $rules }
admin-attachments-overflow = A list holds at most { $max } rules. The rest were not added.
admin-attachments-conflict-blockedOverAllowed = { $rule } overlaps { $other } in the other list. Blocked rules win, so it is blocked.
admin-attachments-conflict-blockedOverWarn = { $rule } overlaps { $other } in the other list. A blocked file is refused before any warning, so the warning never shows.
admin-attachments-conflict-allowedAndWarn = { $rule } overlaps { $other } in the other list. The file is allowed and shows a warning.
admin-attachments-bytes-unit = Unit
admin-attachments-unlimited = No size limit
admin-attachments-bytes-equals = { $size } ({ $bytes } bytes)
admin-attachments-list-allowedExtensions = allowed extensions
admin-attachments-list-allowedMimeTypes = allowed MIME types
admin-attachments-list-blockedExtensions = blocked extensions
admin-attachments-list-blockedMimeTypes = blocked MIME types
admin-attachments-list-warnExtensions = warning extensions
admin-attachments-list-warnMimeTypes = warning MIME types
admin-attachments-sim-title = Test a file
admin-attachments-sim-help = Asks the server how the saved policy treats a file with this name, type and size. Nothing is changed or stored. Messages and attachments are never read.
admin-attachments-sim-filename = File name
admin-attachments-sim-mime = MIME type
admin-attachments-sim-size = Size
admin-attachments-sim-run = Test
admin-attachments-sim-invalid = Enter a file name and a size of zero or more.
admin-attachments-sim-allowed = Allowed
admin-attachments-sim-warn = Allowed with a warning
admin-attachments-sim-blocked = Not delivered
admin-attachments-sim-preview-yes = Preview is allowed.
admin-attachments-sim-preview-no = Preview is not allowed.
admin-attachments-sim-checked = Size checked: { $size }.
admin-attachments-sim-matched = Matched rules in: { $lists }.
admin-attachments-sim-matched-none = No allow, block or warning rule matched.
admin-attachments-reason-downloadsDisabled = Downloads are turned off.
admin-attachments-reason-attachmentTooLarge = The file is larger than the size limit.
admin-attachments-reason-attachmentBlocked = A block rule matches.
admin-attachments-reason-attachmentNotAllowed = An allow list exists and nothing in it matches.
admin-attachments-reason-attachmentContainerRestricted = Attached messages and TNEF files are refused while any restriction is on, because their contents are not listed.

admin-settings-key-mail-reply-images = Images in replies and forwards
admin-settings-help-mail-reply-images = Whether a reply or forward includes the original message's images: ask (default), always allow, allow only for trusted sender domains and ask otherwise, or always deny. Lock this setting to enforce it. Images are only ever read when included.
admin-settings-key-mail-reply-image-trusted-domains = Trusted image sender domains
admin-settings-help-mail-reply-image-trusted-domains = Up to 200 exact sender domains whose images are included without asking when the policy is trusted domains. Users add to their own list from the quote prompt unless this setting is locked.

admin-settings-key-mail-send-recall-delay-seconds = Undo-send window (default)
admin-settings-help-mail-send-recall-delay-seconds = How many seconds a sent message waits in the Outbox, where the sender can recall it, before it is delivered. 0 sends at once. Default 10, up to 1800 (30 minutes). Users choose their own value up to the limit below unless you lock this.
admin-settings-key-mail-send-recall-delay-max-seconds = Undo-send window (limit)
admin-settings-help-mail-send-recall-delay-max-seconds = The longest undo-send window a user may choose, in seconds. The server shortens a longer request to this value. Default and maximum 1800.
admin-settings-key-mail-send-allow-recall = Allow recalling sent messages
admin-settings-help-mail-send-allow-recall = When off, messages leave at once and cannot be recalled from the Outbox. Scheduled sends are not affected; they can still be cancelled until their time.
admin-settings-key-mail-send-max-delayed-seconds = Scheduling horizon
admin-settings-help-mail-send-max-delayed-seconds = How far ahead a message may be scheduled, in seconds. Default 7776000 (90 days), maximum 31536000 (1 year). 0 turns scheduled sending off.
admin-settings-key-mail-send-max-queued = Queued messages per mailbox
admin-settings-help-mail-send-max-queued = How many messages one mailbox may have waiting in the Outbox (undo window or scheduled) at once. Default 200. Further sends are refused with a clear message and are never dropped.
admin-attachments-sim-pick = Fill in from a file (optional)
admin-attachments-mime-toggle = Show common MIME types
admin-attachments-mime-hint = Pick a common type or type any other type/subtype.
admin-attachments-mime-invalid = This is not a type/subtype such as text/plain. It will be sent as typed.
admin-attachments-mime-group-documents = Documents
admin-attachments-mime-group-images = Images
admin-attachments-mime-group-archives = Archives
admin-attachments-mime-group-executables = Executables and scripts
admin-attachments-mime-group-media = Audio and video
admin-attachments-mime-group-email = Email and calendar
admin-attachments-mime-group-other = Other


# Cookie consent
admin-settings-key-cookies-enabled = Cookie consent control
admin-settings-help-cookies-enabled = Show the cookie consent control to visitors. Off keeps the application as it behaves without the control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-mode = Consent model
admin-settings-help-cookies-mode = optIn: nothing optional is stored until the visitor accepts. optOut: category defaults apply until the visitor rejects. noticeOnly: the visitor is informed, with no choice.

admin-settings-key-cookies-region-mode = Consent model in strict regions
admin-settings-help-cookies-region-mode = The model used for visitors in the strict regions. same uses the consent model above there too.

admin-settings-key-cookies-strict-regions = Strict regions
admin-settings-help-cookies-strict-regions = ISO 3166-1 country codes that use the strict-region consent model. Defaults to the EU and EEA states, the United Kingdom and Switzerland.

admin-settings-key-cookies-region-header = Country header
admin-settings-help-cookies-region-header = Name of the request header, set by a proxy or CDN, that holds the visitor country code.

admin-settings-key-cookies-unknown-region = Unknown country
admin-settings-help-cookies-unknown-region = Which model applies when no country can be determined: the strict-region model or the normal one.

admin-settings-key-cookies-functional-enabled = Offer functional cookies
admin-settings-help-cookies-functional-enabled = Offer the preferences and functional category (theme, language, layout memory) in the consent control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-functional-default = Functional default
admin-settings-help-cookies-functional-default = Initial state of the functional category when the consent model allows defaults.

admin-settings-key-cookies-analytics-enabled = Offer analytics cookies
admin-settings-help-cookies-analytics-enabled = Offer the analytics category in the consent control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-analytics-default = Analytics default
admin-settings-help-cookies-analytics-default = Initial state of the analytics category when the consent model allows defaults.

admin-settings-key-cookies-marketing-enabled = Offer marketing cookies
admin-settings-help-cookies-marketing-enabled = Offer the marketing category in the consent control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-marketing-default = Marketing default
admin-settings-help-cookies-marketing-default = Initial state of the marketing category when the consent model allows defaults.

admin-settings-key-cookies-layout = Layout
admin-settings-help-cookies-layout = banner is a bar across the page, card is a floating card, modal is a dialog that holds the page until the visitor chooses.

admin-settings-key-cookies-position = Position
admin-settings-help-cookies-position = Where the consent control appears on the page.

admin-settings-key-cookies-reject-prominent = Reject as prominent as accept
admin-settings-help-cookies-reject-prominent = Show Reject all with the same size and style as Accept all.

admin-settings-key-cookies-policy-url = Cookie policy URL
admin-settings-help-cookies-policy-url = Link to your cookie policy, shown in the consent control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-privacy-url = Privacy policy URL
admin-settings-help-cookies-privacy-url = Link to your privacy policy, shown in the consent control.

admin-settings-key-cookies-policy-version = Policy version
admin-settings-help-cookies-policy-version = Raise this number when your cookie use changes, so visitors are asked again.

admin-settings-key-cookies-lifetime-days = Consent lifetime
admin-settings-help-cookies-lifetime-days = Days a decision stays valid before the visitor is asked again.

admin-settings-key-cookies-reprompt-on-version = Ask again on a new policy version
admin-settings-help-cookies-reprompt-on-version = Ask visitors again when the policy version is higher than the one they decided on.

admin-settings-key-cookies-honour-gpc = Honour Global Privacy Control
admin-settings-help-cookies-honour-gpc = Treat a Global Privacy Control signal from the browser as a rejection of analytics and marketing.

admin-settings-key-cookies-honour-dnt = Honour Do Not Track
admin-settings-help-cookies-honour-dnt = Treat a Do Not Track signal from the browser as a rejection of analytics and marketing.

admin-settings-key-cookies-log-consent = Keep a consent log
admin-settings-help-cookies-log-consent = Keep a server-side record of each consent decision, for statistics and your own records.

admin-settings-key-cookies-log-retention-days = Consent log retention
admin-settings-help-cookies-log-retention-days = Days consent log rows are kept before they are deleted.

admin-settings-key-cookies-scan-interval-hours = Storage scan interval
admin-settings-help-cookies-scan-interval-hours = Hours between automatic scans of the browser's cookies and storage. 0 scans only on demand.

admin-settings-key-cookies-unclassified = Unclassified storage
admin-settings-help-cookies-unclassified = report leaves storage that nothing classifies alone and lists it for review. The other values treat it as that category until you classify it.

admin-settings-key-cookies-text-title = Consent control title
admin-settings-help-cookies-text-title = Title of the consent control per language. Empty uses the built-in text.

admin-settings-key-cookies-text-body = Consent control text
admin-settings-help-cookies-text-body = Explanatory text of the consent control per language. Empty uses the built-in text.

admin-settings-key-cookies-label-necessary = Name of the necessary category
admin-settings-help-cookies-label-necessary = Name of the necessary category per language. Empty uses the built-in name.

admin-settings-key-cookies-description-necessary = Description of the necessary category
admin-settings-help-cookies-description-necessary = Description of the necessary category per language. Empty uses the built-in description.

admin-settings-key-cookies-label-functional = Name of the functional category
admin-settings-help-cookies-label-functional = Name of the functional category per language. Empty uses the built-in name.

admin-settings-key-cookies-description-functional = Description of the functional category
admin-settings-help-cookies-description-functional = Description of the functional category per language. Empty uses the built-in description.

admin-settings-key-cookies-label-analytics = Name of the analytics category
admin-settings-help-cookies-label-analytics = Name of the analytics category per language. Empty uses the built-in name.

admin-settings-key-cookies-description-analytics = Description of the analytics category
admin-settings-help-cookies-description-analytics = Description of the analytics category per language. Empty uses the built-in description.

admin-settings-key-cookies-label-marketing = Name of the marketing category
admin-settings-help-cookies-label-marketing = Name of the marketing category per language. Empty uses the built-in name.

admin-settings-key-cookies-description-marketing = Description of the marketing category
admin-settings-help-cookies-description-marketing = Description of the marketing category per language. Empty uses the built-in description.

admin-settings-key-encryption-rotation-days = Database key rotation interval (days)
admin-settings-help-encryption-rotation-days = Days after the last key change at which the database key is reported as due for rotation. 0 sets no due date. The key itself is never stored in settings.
admin-settings-key-encryption-warnings-enabled = Report encryption findings
admin-settings-help-encryption-warnings-enabled = Show plaintext stores and an overdue key rotation as a finding in the deployment assessment.
admin-settings-key-retention-sweeper-enabled = Retention sweeper
admin-settings-help-retention-sweeper-enabled = Run the daily sweep that deletes rows older than the limits on this page. Turning it off keeps every row until it is turned on again.
admin-settings-key-retention-sweeper-batch-rows = Rows per batch
admin-settings-help-retention-sweeper-batch-rows = Rows one delete statement removes. Smaller batches hold database locks for less time.
admin-settings-key-retention-sweeper-max-batches = Batches per store per run
admin-settings-help-retention-sweeper-max-batches = Most delete statements one store gets in a run. A store with more old rows continues in the next run.
admin-settings-key-retention-sweeper-jitter-minutes = Start-time spread (minutes)
admin-settings-help-retention-sweeper-jitter-minutes = The next run starts a random number of minutes up to this value after 24 hours, so several servers do not sweep together.
admin-settings-key-retention-sweeper-vacuum-after-rows = Reclaim space after (rows)
admin-settings-help-retention-sweeper-vacuum-after-rows = When one run deletes at least this many rows the database is compacted (VACUUM). 0 never compacts after a sweep; the weekly vacuum job is separate.
admin-settings-key-retention-password-change-audit-days = Password-change records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-password-change-audit-days = Days a password-change record (account, method, outcome) is kept. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-sso-login-audit-days = Single sign-on login records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-sso-login-audit-days = Days a single sign-on login record (provider, hashed subject, outcome) is kept. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-dlp-audit-days = Data-loss-prevention records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-dlp-audit-days = Days a record of a data-loss-prevention rule match is kept. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-assist-audit-days = Assistant access records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-assist-audit-days = Days a record of an assistant using a capability (actor, capability, scope summary) is kept. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-alert-events-days = Fired alert records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-alert-events-days = Days a record of a fired administrator alert is kept. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-job-runs-days = Background job history (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-job-runs-days = Days a finished background-job run is kept. A run that is still running is never removed. 0 keeps the history forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-outbox-days = Sent and cancelled send records (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-outbox-days = Days the send record of a delivered or cancelled message is kept. A message that is waiting, being retried, failed or uncertain is never removed. 0 keeps them forever.
admin-settings-key-retention-expired-credentials-grace-days = Expired credentials (days after expiry)
admin-settings-help-retention-expired-credentials-grace-days = Days an expired remembered device, sign-in challenge, sign-in token, OAuth token, webhook nonce, source failure counter or image link handle is kept after it expired. 0 removes it on the next run.
admin-settings-key-retention-ip-addresses-days = Reduce stored IP addresses after (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-ip-addresses-days = After this many days the IP address in authentication history and audit entries is truncated or hashed and the row is kept. 0 keeps addresses as recorded.
admin-settings-key-retention-ip-addresses-mode = IP reduction method
admin-settings-help-retention-ip-addresses-mode = Truncate keeps the IPv4 /24 or IPv6 /48 prefix. Hash replaces the address with a short keyed hash that still groups the same address.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-enabled = Users may set retention rules
admin-settings-help-retention-user-enabled = Users can set their own retention rules for folders and mail. When off, existing user rules stop running; the organisation-wide rules below still run.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-min-days = Fewest days before a user rule deletes mail
admin-settings-help-retention-user-min-days = A user rule that deletes mail cannot act on mail younger than this. A smaller value is refused when the rule is saved and raised when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-max-days = Most days a user rule may wait to delete mail
admin-settings-help-retention-user-max-days = A user rule that deletes mail cannot wait longer than this. 0 sets no ceiling. A larger value is refused when the rule is saved and lowered when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-max-rules = Most retention rules per user
admin-settings-help-retention-user-max-rules = The most retention rules one user may keep.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-allow-permanent-delete = User rules may delete mail permanently
admin-settings-help-retention-user-allow-permanent-delete = When off, a delete rule always moves mail to Trash and the undo window applies before it is purged.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-undo-days = Undo window for retention rules (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-user-undo-days = Days mail moved to Trash by a retention rule stays there before it is purged. A user may choose a shorter window. 0 purges at the next run.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-mandatory = Organisation-wide mail rules
admin-settings-help-retention-user-mandatory = Rules every account gets, as folder-role:days entries, for example trash:30 or junk:30. Mail in that folder older than the days is purged. A user cannot change, pause or exclude mail from these. Mail of an account under legal hold is skipped.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-protected-folders = Folders retention rules never touch
admin-settings-help-retention-user-protected-folders = Folders no user rule works on, by role (drafts, sent, inbox, archive) or by folder name. A protected folder wins over an organisation-wide rule for the same folder.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-templates = Retention templates offered to users
admin-settings-help-retention-user-templates = Templates users can adopt in Settings, by id: newsletters30, receipts365, notifications14, trash30, junk30, read-archive180.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-run-for-restricted = Run user rules for restricted accounts
admin-settings-help-retention-user-run-for-restricted = Whether user retention rules also run for accounts under a restriction of processing. Off skips those accounts.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-interval-hours = Hours between user retention runs
admin-settings-help-retention-user-interval-hours = Hours between scheduled runs of the user retention job for one account.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-batch-messages = Messages per retention call
admin-settings-help-retention-user-batch-messages = Messages one move or delete call handles. At most 200 are used.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-max-per-run = Most messages changed per account per run
admin-settings-help-retention-user-max-per-run = Most messages the user retention job changes for one account in one run. The rest waits for the next run.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-pause-ms = Pause between retention batches (ms)
admin-settings-help-retention-user-pause-ms = Pause between batches, in milliseconds, so a large cleanup does not load the mail server.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-allow-strip-attachments = Users may remove attachments from old mail
admin-settings-help-retention-user-allow-strip-attachments = Whether users may create rules that remove large attachments from old mail. Off by default. While off, the action is hidden in the rule editor, a rule that uses it is refused when saved, and rules saved earlier are skipped when the job runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-strip-min-age-days = Fewest days before attachments are removed
admin-settings-help-retention-user-strip-min-age-days = Fewest days a message must be old before a rule may remove its attachments. A smaller value is refused when the rule is saved and raised when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-strip-min-attachment-kb = Smallest attachment removed (KB)
admin-settings-help-retention-user-strip-min-attachment-kb = Only attachments at least this size are removed. Smaller attachments stay with the message.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-strip-keep-inline-images = Keep inline images
admin-settings-help-retention-user-strip-keep-inline-images = Whether images shown inside the message body are kept when attachments are removed.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-strip-undo-days = Undo window after attachments are removed (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-user-strip-undo-days = Days the original message stays in Trash after its attachments were removed. -1 follows the undo window for retention rules. 0 deletes the original at once.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-calendar-enabled = Users may delete ended calendar events
admin-settings-help-retention-user-calendar-enabled = Whether users may choose calendars whose events are deleted a set number of days after they ended. Off by default. While off, the option is hidden in Settings, a choice is refused when saved, and choices saved earlier are not run.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-calendar-min-days = Fewest days before ended events are deleted
admin-settings-help-retention-user-calendar-min-days = Fewest days after an event ended before a user rule may delete it. A smaller value is refused when saved and raised when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-calendar-max-days = Most days before ended events are deleted
admin-settings-help-retention-user-calendar-max-days = Most days a user may wait before ended events are deleted. A larger value is refused when saved and lowered when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-notes-enabled = Users may remove untouched notes
admin-settings-help-retention-user-notes-enabled = Whether users may choose to remove notes not changed for a set number of days. Off by default. Removed notes can be restored until the undo window for retention rules ends.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-notes-min-days = Fewest days before untouched notes are removed
admin-settings-help-retention-user-notes-min-days = Fewest days a note must be untouched before a user rule may remove it. A smaller value is refused when saved and raised when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-user-notes-max-days = Most days before untouched notes are removed
admin-settings-help-retention-user-notes-max-days = Most days a user may wait before untouched notes are removed. A larger value is refused when saved and lowered when it runs.
admin-settings-key-retention-class-short-days = Short class ceiling (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-class-short-days = Ceiling for operational data: sessions, tokens, rate limits, job history and metrics. Applies when the class limit is on.
admin-settings-key-retention-class-medium-days = Medium class ceiling (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-class-medium-days = Ceiling for sign-in history, request protection history and security notices. Must not be below the short class; a lower value is raised to it.
admin-settings-key-retention-class-long-days = Long class retention (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-class-long-days = Days the long class (security audit, administrator actions, requests, consent, tombstones) is kept, archive included. 0 keeps it for ever and the console warns. Must not be below the medium class.
admin-settings-key-retention-class-enforce = Hold each store to its class ceiling
admin-settings-help-retention-class-enforce = When on, each store's own limit is clamped to its class ceiling and 0 (keep) counts as the ceiling. When off, per-store limits stand.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-enabled = Archive aged rows of the long class
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-enabled = Move aged rows of the long class into sealed, compressed archive files instead of deleting them.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-directory = Archive directory
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-directory = Directory for archive files, absolute or relative to the server working directory. Parent-directory segments (..) are refused.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-batch-rows = Rows per archive file
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-batch-rows = Rows written into one archive file.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-max-segments = Archive files per store per run
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-max-segments = Archive files one run may write for each store. The rest waits for the next run.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-key-generation = Archive sealing key generation
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-key-generation = Generation of the key that seals new archive files. Raise it to rotate the key; earlier files still verify with their own generation.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-verify-days = Days between archive checks
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-verify-days = Days between integrity checks of the archive files.
admin-settings-key-retention-archive-legal-hold = Legal hold on the archive
admin-settings-help-retention-archive-legal-hold = Keep every archive file, whatever the long class limit says.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-enabled = Write log files
admin-settings-help-logging-file-enabled = Also write the server log to rotating files. Off keeps logging to standard output only, which is what a container normally uses.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-directory = Log directory
admin-settings-help-logging-file-directory = Directory for the log files, absolute or relative to the server's working directory. Parent-directory segments (..) are refused.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-max-size-mb = Rotate at size (MB)
admin-settings-help-logging-file-max-size-mb = The current log file is closed and a new one started when it reaches this size.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-rotate-hours = Rotate at age (hours)
admin-settings-help-logging-file-rotate-hours = The current log file is rotated once it is this old. 0 rotates by size only.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-max-age-days = Keep rotated files (days)
admin-settings-help-logging-file-max-age-days = Rotated log files older than this are deleted.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-max-files = Most rotated files
admin-settings-help-logging-file-max-files = The oldest rotated files beyond this count are deleted.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-max-total-mb = Most total size (MB)
admin-settings-help-logging-file-max-total-mb = The oldest rotated files are deleted until the log directory is under this size.
admin-settings-key-logging-file-compress = Compress rotated files
admin-settings-help-logging-file-compress = Rotated log files are compressed with gzip.
admin-settings-key-logging-level = Log level
admin-settings-help-logging-level = The level for components that have no level of their own below. The MW_LOG environment variable sets the level at start-up until this setting is read.
admin-settings-key-logging-component-levels = Component log levels
admin-settings-help-logging-component-levels = One component=level entry per line, for example mw_imap=debug. Levels are error, warn, info, debug and trace.
admin-settings-key-logging-redaction-addresses = Email addresses in logs
admin-settings-help-logging-redaction-addresses = Full leaves addresses as logged. Truncated keeps the first letter and the domain. Hashed replaces the local part with a short hash. None removes the address.
admin-settings-key-logging-redaction-ips = IP addresses in logs
admin-settings-help-logging-redaction-ips = Full leaves addresses as logged. Truncated keeps the IPv4 /24 or IPv6 /48 prefix. Hashed replaces the address with a short hash. None removes it.
admin-settings-key-logging-redaction-tokens = Secrets in logs
admin-settings-help-logging-redaction-tokens = Cuts bearer tokens, API keys, passwords in URLs and similar secrets out of log lines.
admin-settings-key-retention-sessions-idle-days = Unused sessions (days)
admin-settings-help-retention-sessions-idle-days = Days a browser or native-client session record, with its address and user agent, may go unused before it is deleted. The session timeouts apply first; this only removes rows left behind. 0 keeps them.

admin-settings-key-policy-public-pages = Public policy pages
admin-settings-help-policy-public-pages = Serve the generated privacy policy at /privacy and cookie policy at /cookies-policy without sign-in.
admin-settings-key-policy-auto-version = Automatic policy versions
admin-settings-help-policy-auto-version = Record a new policy version when a setting the policy describes changes. Off: changes wait for Publish.
admin-settings-key-policy-reconsent-on-change = Ask for cookie consent again on a new policy version
admin-settings-help-policy-reconsent-on-change = Raise the cookie policy version when a new policy version is recorded, so visitors are asked again (needs cookies.repromptOnVersion).
admin-settings-key-policy-controller-name = Controller name
admin-settings-help-policy-controller-name = Name of the organisation that decides why and how data is processed, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-policy-controller-address = Controller address
admin-settings-help-policy-controller-address = Postal address of the controller, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-policy-legal-bases = Legal bases
admin-settings-help-policy-legal-bases = The legal bases you rely on, in your own words, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-policy-hosting-provider = Hosting provider
admin-settings-help-policy-hosting-provider = Who hosts the data and where, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-policy-hosting-transfers = Transfers outside the hosting country
admin-settings-help-policy-hosting-transfers = Any transfers of data to other countries and the safeguards you use, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-policy-supervisory-authority = Supervisory authority
admin-settings-help-policy-supervisory-authority = The authority users may complain to, shown in the privacy policy.
admin-settings-key-dpia-suggest = Suggest impact assessments
admin-settings-help-dpia-suggest = List a suggested impact assessment when the assistant, open tracking or analytics is enabled and none exists.
admin-settings-key-dpia-review-months = Impact assessment review interval
admin-settings-help-dpia-review-months = Months until the review date set when an assessment is approved.
admin-settings-key-dpia-reminder-days = Impact assessment reminder window
admin-settings-help-dpia-reminder-days = Days before the review date that an assessment is listed as due.
admin-settings-key-restriction-enabled = Restrictions of processing
admin-settings-help-restriction-enabled = Whether an administrator or an approved request can restrict processing of a person's data.
admin-settings-key-restriction-auto-apply-on-approval = Restrict when a request is approved
admin-settings-help-restriction-auto-apply-on-approval = Apply the restriction as soon as a restriction request is approved. Off: an administrator applies it from Compliance > Restrictions.
admin-settings-key-restriction-mail-delivery = New mail while restricted
admin-settings-help-restriction-mail-delivery = What the administrator chose for mail that arrives while a restriction applies: keep it, queue it or reject it. This server does not receive mail; the value is recorded and shown, and the mail server acts on it.
admin-settings-key-restriction-default-expiry-days = Default restriction length (days)
admin-settings-help-restriction-default-expiry-days = Days until a new restriction ends by itself. 0 keeps it until someone lifts it.
admin-settings-key-restriction-notify-user = Tell the person
admin-settings-help-restriction-notify-user = Send the person a notice when a restriction is applied or lifted.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-indexing = Pause search indexing and embeddings
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-indexing = Whether search indexing and embeddings is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-assistant = Pause the assistant
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-assistant = Whether the assistant is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-analytics = Pause analytics and open tracking
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-analytics = Whether analytics and open tracking is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-classification = Pause rules and automatic filing
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-classification = Whether rules and automatic filing is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-push = Pause push notifications
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-push = Whether push notifications is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-restriction-scope-third-party = Pause connected services and plugins
admin-settings-help-restriction-scope-third-party = Whether connected services and plugins is paused by default in a new restriction.
admin-settings-key-consent-enabled = Purpose consent
admin-settings-help-consent-enabled = Show purposes and consent choices to users and enforce them at runtime.
admin-settings-key-consent-receipts-retention-days = Consent receipts kept (days)
admin-settings-help-consent-receipts-retention-days = Days consent receipts are kept. 0 keeps them until the person is erased.
admin-settings-key-consent-art22-notice = Automated processing notice
admin-settings-help-consent-art22-notice = Show users the plain-language notice about assistant and search features, with the per-feature switches.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-basis = Legal basis: usage counts
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-basis = The legal basis shown to users for usage counts. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-version = Text version: usage counts
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-text = Own wording: usage counts
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-tag-basis = Legal basis: analytics provider script
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-tag-basis = The legal basis shown to users for analytics provider script. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-tag-version = Text version: analytics provider script
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-tag-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-analytics-tag-text = Own wording: analytics provider script
admin-settings-help-consent-analytics-tag-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-assistant-basis = Legal basis: assistant
admin-settings-help-consent-assistant-basis = The legal basis shown to users for assistant. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-assistant-version = Text version: assistant
admin-settings-help-consent-assistant-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-assistant-text = Own wording: assistant
admin-settings-help-consent-assistant-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-push-basis = Legal basis: push notifications
admin-settings-help-consent-push-basis = The legal basis shown to users for push notifications. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-push-version = Text version: push notifications
admin-settings-help-consent-push-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-push-text = Own wording: push notifications
admin-settings-help-consent-push-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-open-tracking-basis = Legal basis: open tracking
admin-settings-help-consent-open-tracking-basis = The legal basis shown to users for open tracking. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-open-tracking-version = Text version: open tracking
admin-settings-help-consent-open-tracking-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-open-tracking-text = Own wording: open tracking
admin-settings-help-consent-open-tracking-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-remote-content-basis = Legal basis: remote images
admin-settings-help-consent-remote-content-basis = The legal basis shown to users for remote images. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-remote-content-version = Text version: remote images
admin-settings-help-consent-remote-content-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-remote-content-text = Own wording: remote images
admin-settings-help-consent-remote-content-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-integrations-basis = Legal basis: connected services
admin-settings-help-consent-integrations-basis = The legal basis shown to users for connected services. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-integrations-version = Text version: connected services
admin-settings-help-consent-integrations-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-integrations-text = Own wording: connected services
admin-settings-help-consent-integrations-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-consent-telemetry-basis = Legal basis: load-time measurements
admin-settings-help-consent-telemetry-basis = The legal basis shown to users for load-time measurements. Only consent makes the feature wait for a yes; the other bases apply unless the person withdraws. The administrator decides which basis is right.
admin-settings-key-consent-telemetry-version = Text version: load-time measurements
admin-settings-help-consent-telemetry-version = Raise this number when the wording or the processing changes; people who agreed to an older version are asked again.
admin-settings-key-consent-telemetry-text = Own wording: load-time measurements
admin-settings-help-consent-telemetry-text = Your own text for this purpose, per language. Empty uses the built-in wording.
admin-settings-key-breach-enabled = Breach register
admin-settings-help-breach-enabled = Switches the register and the notice clock on.
admin-settings-key-breach-notice-hours = Hours to notify the authority
admin-settings-help-breach-notice-hours = Hours from becoming aware to the authority notice. The usual window is 72.
admin-settings-key-breach-reminders-hours = Reminder times
admin-settings-help-breach-reminders-hours = Hours before the deadline that raise a reminder, for example 6, 24 and 48.
admin-settings-key-breach-reminders-overdue-repeat-hours = Overdue repeat
admin-settings-help-breach-reminders-overdue-repeat-hours = Hours between reminders once the deadline has passed. 0 reminds once.
admin-settings-key-breach-authority-name = Supervisory authority
admin-settings-help-breach-authority-name = Name printed on the authority notice.
admin-settings-key-breach-authority-url = Authority notification page
admin-settings-help-breach-authority-url = Address of the authority's notification page.
admin-settings-key-breach-authority-contact = Authority contact
admin-settings-help-breach-authority-contact = Contact details of the authority.
admin-settings-key-breach-dpo-name = Data protection contact name
admin-settings-help-breach-dpo-name = Name given as the contact point in notices.
admin-settings-key-breach-dpo-email = Data protection contact email
admin-settings-help-breach-dpo-email = Address given as the contact point in notices.
admin-settings-key-breach-dpo-phone = Data protection contact phone
admin-settings-help-breach-dpo-phone = Phone number given in notices.
admin-settings-key-breach-template-subject = Message subject
admin-settings-help-breach-template-subject = Subject of the message to people affected, per language.
admin-settings-key-breach-template-body = Message text
admin-settings-help-breach-template-body = Text of the message to people affected, per language.
admin-settings-key-breach-notify-audit = Record notices in the audit log
admin-settings-help-breach-notify-audit = Reminders and detections become security events.
admin-settings-key-breach-notify-webhook-urls = Webhook addresses
admin-settings-help-breach-notify-webhook-urls = Addresses told about reminders and messages. Treat them as secrets; each call is signed.
admin-settings-key-breach-notify-operator-addresses = Operator mailboxes
admin-settings-help-breach-notify-operator-addresses = Local mailbox addresses that receive reminders in their own inbox.
admin-settings-key-breach-subjects-in-app = Notice in the person's account
admin-settings-help-breach-subjects-in-app = Show the message inside the person's account.
admin-settings-key-breach-subjects-inbox = Message to the person's mailbox
admin-settings-help-breach-subjects-inbox = Deliver the message to the person's own mailbox.
admin-settings-key-breach-subjects-webhook = Also send to webhooks
admin-settings-help-breach-subjects-webhook = Send the message text to the webhook addresses too.
admin-settings-key-breach-retention-years = Register retention in years
admin-settings-help-breach-retention-years = Years a closed incident stays in the register.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-enabled = Automations
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-enabled = Open draft incidents from detections.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-start-clock = Draft clock
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-start-clock = Start the clock when the draft opens, or only when it is confirmed.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-assignee = Assign drafts to
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-assignee = Who a draft is assigned to.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-escalate-after-hours = Escalate after hours
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-escalate-after-hours = Hours a draft waits before it is escalated. 0 never escalates.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-escalate-to = Escalate to
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-escalate-to = Who an escalated draft is assigned to.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-window-minutes = Counting window in minutes
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-window-minutes = Minutes over which a rule counts events.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-theft-threshold = Session theft alerts
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-theft-threshold = Alerts in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-credential-stuffing-threshold = Sign-in spray or spike
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-credential-stuffing-threshold = Events in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-mass-forward-threshold = Forwarding rules in bulk
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-mass-forward-threshold = Events in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-role-escalation-threshold = Administrator role changes
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-role-escalation-threshold = Changes in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-export-volume-threshold = Unusual exports
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-export-volume-threshold = Exports in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-audit-chain-threshold = Audit chain failures
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-audit-chain-threshold = Failures that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-backup-anomaly-threshold = Backup or restore failures
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-backup-anomaly-threshold = Failures in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-breach-auto-dsr-export-threshold = Many data request exports
admin-settings-help-breach-auto-dsr-export-threshold = Exports in the window that open a draft. 0 is off.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-queue-ms = Longest wait for a free slot
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-queue-ms = Longest a request waits for a free slot (JMAP concurrency, image decoders, preview workers) before it is refused with 429 and Retry-After. Range 0-30000 ms; default 3000. Zero refuses at once.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-jmap-per-account-concurrent = JMAP requests at once per account
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-jmap-per-account-concurrent = JMAP requests one signed-in account may run at once, across its tabs and devices. It is never shared with another account or another user behind the same address. Range 4-64; default 8.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-jmap-global-concurrent = JMAP requests at once, all accounts
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-jmap-global-concurrent = JMAP requests the whole server process runs at once, all accounts together. A request over it waits for the queue time. Range 4-4096; default 256.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-session-burst = Timing reports per session in a row
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-session-burst = Client timing reports one session may send in a row. The endpoint is keyed by session, never by address. Range 1-1000; default 60.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-session-per-minute = Timing reports regained per minute
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-session-per-minute = Client timing reports per minute a session regains after its burst. Range 1-600; default 30.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-anon-burst = Anonymous consent requests in a row
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-anon-burst = Requests one address may make to the anonymous cookie-consent routes in a row. Sized for an office behind one address. Range 1-1000; default 60.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-anon-per-minute = Anonymous consent requests regained per minute
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-anon-per-minute = Requests per minute an address regains on the anonymous cookie-consent routes. Range 1-600; default 30.
admin-settings-key-ratelimit-trusted-multiplier = Account allowance from a known source (%)
admin-settings-help-ratelimit-trusted-multiplier = Percentage of the account request allowance a signed-in mailbox gets when the request comes from a source with a successful sign-in on record. 100 keeps the base allowance. It never relaxes the anonymous, administrator or user-agent budgets or an active block. Range 100-1000; default 150.
admin-settings-key-mail-priority-marks = Priority marks
admin-settings-help-mail-priority-marks = Which priority marks the message list, conversations and reader show: both high and low, high only, or none. Users choose under Settings > Folders and sidebar unless locked.
admin-settings-key-mail-priority-marks-style = Priority mark style
admin-settings-help-mail-priority-marks-style = How a priority mark looks: an icon, an icon with the words High or Low, or a thin bar. Icon and text keep the meaning without colour.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-priority-enabled = Priority selector in the composer
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-priority-enabled = Show the Normal, High and Low priority selector in the composer Options group. When off, new mail is sent without priority headers.
admin-settings-key-mail-compose-priority-default = Default message priority
admin-settings-help-mail-compose-priority-default = The priority a new message starts with in the composer.
admin-settings-key-mail-priority-send-headers = Priority headers written on send
admin-settings-help-mail-priority-send-headers = Which headers a high or low priority message gets when sent: any of Importance, X-Priority and X-MSMail-Priority.
admin-settings-key-mail-priority-trust-sender-headers = Trust sender-set priority
admin-settings-help-mail-priority-trust-sender-headers = Whether a priority the sender set is shown: always, only when the message passed an aligned DMARC check, or never. Use trusted or never against senders who mark every message high priority.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-enabled = Folder properties dialog
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-enabled = Offer Properties in the folder menus and on the shortcut. When off, the dialog is not available.
admin-settings-key-properties-message-enabled = Message properties dialog
admin-settings-help-properties-message-enabled = Offer Properties in the message menus and on the shortcut. When off, the dialog is not available.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-sections = Folder dialog sections
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-sections = The sections of the folder Properties dialog: general, remote, size, offline, overrides, notes, actions. A section not listed is hidden.
admin-settings-key-properties-message-sections = Message dialog sections
admin-settings-help-properties-message-sections = The sections of the message Properties dialog: summary, scoring, headers, attachments, actions. A section not listed is hidden.
admin-settings-key-properties-remote-location-visibility = Remote location detail
admin-settings-help-properties-remote-location-visibility = How much of the server-side location users see: full (host and path), masked-host (host partly hidden), path-only (mailbox path without the host), or hidden.
admin-settings-key-properties-headers-raw = Raw headers
admin-settings-help-properties-headers-raw = Allow the message Properties dialog to list the raw headers. When off, only the parsed summary shows.
admin-settings-key-properties-scoring-show = Scoring and authentication details
admin-settings-help-properties-scoring-show = Show spam score, authentication results and security signals in the message Properties dialog.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-overrides-allowed = Per-folder overrides allowed
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-overrides-allowed = Which settings a user may override for a single folder. An override not listed is hidden and any stored value is ignored.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-notes-enabled = Folder notes
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-notes-enabled = Allow a description or note on each folder.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-notes-max-length = Folder note length
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-notes-max-length = The most characters a folder note may hold.
admin-settings-key-properties-folder-size-compute = Folder size computation
admin-settings-help-properties-folder-size-compute = When the size of a folder on the server is worked out: never, when the dialog opens, or in the background. Counting a large mailbox costs the server a scan.
admin-settings-key-properties-offline-clear-enabled = Clear offline cache per folder
admin-settings-help-properties-offline-clear-enabled = Allow users to clear the offline cache of a single folder from its Properties dialog.
admin-settings-key-export-folder-enabled = Folder export
admin-settings-help-export-folder-enabled = Allow users to download a whole folder as a ZIP of messages. Each export is audited.
admin-settings-key-export-folder-format = Folder export format
admin-settings-help-export-folder-format = The formats a folder export offers: a ZIP of .eml files, a ZIP holding an mbox file, or both.
admin-settings-key-export-folder-max-bytes = Folder export size limit
admin-settings-help-export-folder-max-bytes = The most bytes of messages one folder export may hold. A larger folder is refused with the size shown.
admin-settings-key-export-folder-max-messages = Folder export message limit
admin-settings-help-export-folder-max-messages = The most messages one folder export may hold.
admin-settings-key-export-folder-include-subfolders = Include subfolders in export
admin-settings-help-export-folder-include-subfolders = Whether a folder export includes its subfolders by default, kept as a folder structure in the ZIP.
admin-settings-key-export-dialog-enabled = Export dialog
admin-settings-help-export-dialog-enabled = Export in the message view and the message menus opens a dialog in place. When off, those menus download the one message as .eml.
admin-settings-key-export-formats = Export dialog formats
admin-settings-help-export-formats = The formats the export dialog offers: eml, mbox, txt, md, msg, docx, csv, json, pdf. The server refuses a listed-out server-built format.
admin-settings-key-export-default-format = Export dialog default format
admin-settings-help-export-default-format = The format the export dialog starts with.
admin-settings-key-export-default-scope = Export dialog default scope
admin-settings-help-export-default-scope = The scope the export dialog starts with: message, conversation, selection or folder.
admin-settings-key-export-message-download-enabled = Message download
admin-settings-help-export-message-download-enabled = Allow users to download a message as .eml, its headers only, or as an mbox file.
admin-settings-key-properties-message-permanent-delete = Permanent delete from properties
admin-settings-help-properties-message-permanent-delete = Whether the message dialog may delete a message for good: allow, ask twice, or deny. A message under legal hold is never deleted. Deleting this way cannot be undone.
admin-settings-key-properties-shortcut-enabled = Properties shortcut
admin-settings-help-properties-shortcut-enabled = Open the Properties dialog from the keyboard on a focused folder or selected message.
admin-settings-key-properties-shortcut-key = Properties shortcut key
admin-settings-help-properties-shortcut-key = The key combination that opens Properties; Alt+Enter by default.
admin-settings-key-attachments-bar-click-to-toggle = Click the attachments bar to toggle
admin-settings-help-attachments-bar-click-to-toggle = Whether clicking anywhere on the reader's attachments bar expands or collapses it. When off, only the arrow button does.
admin-settings-key-attachments-bar-show-download-buttons = Attachment download buttons
admin-settings-help-attachments-bar-show-download-buttons = When each attachment in the bar shows its download button: on hover or focus (default), always, or never. Downloads still follow the attachment policy and mail.allowDownload.
admin-settings-key-attachments-bar-download-all = Download all button
admin-settings-help-attachments-bar-download-all = Whether the attachments bar offers a Download all button that saves the allowed attachments as one ZIP file.
admin-settings-key-attachments-bar-zip-inline-images = Inline images in the Download all ZIP
admin-settings-help-attachments-bar-zip-inline-images = Whether images shown inside the message text are included in the Download all ZIP. Off by default.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-auth = Authentication badge
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-auth = When the reader header shows the DMARC authentication badge: always, only when notable, or never.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-spam = Spam score badge
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-spam = When the reader header shows the spam score badge: always, only when notable, or never.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-sanitized = Sanitized HTML badge
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-sanitized = When the reader header shows the sanitized HTML badge: always, only when notable, or never.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-folder = Folder badge
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-folder = When the reader header shows the folder badge: always, only when notable, or never.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-list = Mailing list badge
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-list = When the reader header shows the mailing list badge: always, only when notable, or never. It needs a List-Id or List-Unsubscribe header.
admin-settings-key-mail-list-unsubscribe-mode = Mailing list Unsubscribe
admin-settings-help-mail-list-unsubscribe-mode = How Unsubscribe works when a list offers a one-click request: ask first, send it at once, or only open the list's link or draft.
admin-settings-key-mail-list-keep = Always keep
admin-settings-help-mail-list-keep = Senders and mailing lists always kept, one per line as sender:address or list:List-Id. Clean up this sender, unsubscribe suggestions and retention rules skip them.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-density = Reader badge size
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-density = Size of the badges in the reader header: compact or comfortable.
admin-settings-key-mail-badge-labels = Reader badge labels
admin-settings-help-mail-badge-labels = Whether reader header badges show an icon with text, or the icon only.

admin-settings-key-mail-search-default-scope = Default mail search scope
admin-settings-help-mail-search-default-scope = Start new normal mail searches in the current folder or across all folders. This controls the initial default, including when locked; users can still choose a different scope for a particular search. Saved and explicitly scoped queries are preserved.

admin-settings-key-mail-message-list-group = Message grouping

admin-settings-help-mail-message-list-group = Group conversations by received or sent date, sender, subject, importance or size. Users may override this unless locked.

admin-settings-key-cap-reading-delete-sender = Allow deleting all mail from a sender

admin-settings-help-cap-reading-delete-sender = Allow users to enable the reader action that moves all matching sender messages to Trash after confirmation. Disabled by default. The feature profile must also permit it.

admin-settings-key-reader-actions-delete-sender = Delete all messages from sender action

admin-settings-help-reader-actions-delete-sender = Hidden by default. Choose toolbar or More menu to enable it when the sender-delete capability and feature profile allow it. Users may override placement unless locked.

admin-settings-key-reader-actions-finish-followup = Mark follow-up as finished action

admin-settings-help-reader-actions-finish-followup = Choose toolbar, More menu or hidden for completing flagged messages and follow-up reminders.

admin-settings-key-mail-cache-keep-indefinitely = Keep browser mail cache indefinitely
admin-settings-help-mail-cache-keep-indefinitely = Off by default. Save encrypted account-scoped mail snapshots across browser reloads without age expiry. Existing entry and byte limits still apply. Users can clear saved copies; disabling this preference removes them on the active browser. This does not grant browser persistent-storage permission or download attachments.
admin-settings-key-mail-conversations-allowed = Make conversation threading available
admin-settings-help-mail-conversations-allowed = Allow users to group related replies into conversations. Available by default, but the user preference starts off. Disabling availability overrides the user's choice without changing category grouping.
admin-settings-key-mail-conversations-enabled = Group messages into conversations
admin-settings-help-mail-conversations-enabled = Off by default. Group loaded replies by thread, independently of Group by. Set the default or lock this preference. Conversation availability must also be enabled.

admin-settings-key-links-trusted-sender-domains = Trusted sender domains for message links
admin-settings-help-links-trusted-sender-domains = Up to 100 exact lowercase sender domains whose reviewed message links are enabled automatically. Subdomains are separate. This does not trust destination websites or allow remote images. Empty by default; users can change it unless locked.

admin-settings-key-reader-attachment-action-style = Attachment preview actions
admin-settings-help-reader-attachment-action-style = Show Download and File details beside the preview title as icons (default), labels, or icons and labels. Can be set and locked globally, per domain, or per user.
admin-settings-key-reader-attachment-thumbnails = Image attachment thumbnails
admin-settings-help-reader-attachment-thumbnails = Off by default. Allow visible image attachments to load thumbnail previews. Attachment security rules still apply. Can be set and locked globally, per domain, or per user.
admin-settings-key-retention-image-handles-grace-days = Expired image handle retention
admin-settings-help-retention-image-handles-grace-days = Days expired image handles are kept before cleanup. Zero removes them after expiry.
admin-settings-key-mail-templates-show-in-sidebar = Show Templates in the sidebar
admin-settings-help-mail-templates-show-in-sidebar = Show the Templates workspace in the mailbox sidebar while templates are enabled. Administrators can set and lock the preference.
admin-settings-key-folders-colour = Default folder colour
admin-settings-help-folders-colour = Set a #RRGGBB colour for folder icons and names. Clear the value to follow the theme. Lock it to prevent individual overrides.
admin-settings-key-reader-actions-create-task = Create task action
admin-settings-help-reader-actions-create-task = Choose toolbar, More menu or hidden for creating a task from a message.
admin-settings-key-receipts-schedule-allowed = Scheduled read receipts
admin-settings-help-receipts-schedule-allowed = Allow users to schedule requested read receipts for a message or sender.
